WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:47.660 align:middle line:90%


00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:48.410 align:middle line:90%
OK, Larry.

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:53.090 align:middle line:84%
Let's go ahead now with
the rest of your story.

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:56.540 align:middle line:84%
And pick up where we stopped
with the army service.

00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:57.800 align:middle line:90%
Yes, I'm in the army.

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:01.730 align:middle line:84%
And like I said before,
I created a little bit

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:04.129 align:middle line:90%
of a hardcore around myself.

00:01:04.129 --> 00:01:09.320 align:middle line:84%
And we found out that
the ghetto does not have

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:13.700 align:middle line:90%
bread for two days already.

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:16.430 align:middle line:90%
And there is no sign.

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:19.610 align:middle line:84%
We're not permitted to
leave to go out and buy,

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:24.560 align:middle line:84%
or there is no sign of
improvement at this point.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:27.020 align:middle line:90%
So I called in some of my guys.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:32.720 align:middle line:84%
And we sit down and,
what can we help?

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:34.100 align:middle line:84%
The decision was
made that we are

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:39.440 align:middle line:84%
going to see if we can take
bread from our soldiers, what

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:43.580 align:middle line:84%
we have from our Jewish boys,
and deliver to the ghetto.

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:46.830 align:middle line:90%


00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:51.600 align:middle line:84%
Somehow, the word
got to the general

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:54.060 align:middle line:84%
that we are planning
to take some bread.

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:57.820 align:middle line:90%


00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:01.360 align:middle line:84%
The word got to
him was like this.

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:03.970 align:middle line:90%
We got up early in the morning.

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:07.720 align:middle line:84%
And we packed a
wagon full of bread,

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:10.780 align:middle line:84%
and we threw hay and
straw on top of it,

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:15.220 align:middle line:84%
and put those forks
in it, to make

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:18.970 align:middle line:84%
it look like we are
traveling to deliver hay

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:20.980 align:middle line:90%
to another section of the city.

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:23.230 align:middle line:84%
And two guys got on
the top and drove out.

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:27.760 align:middle line:84%
But one of the sergeants
observed it, and saw everything

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:28.540 align:middle line:90%
we are doing.

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:30.490 align:middle line:84%
So he went to the
general and told him

00:02:30.490 --> 00:02:35.177 align:middle line:84%
that the Jew boys stole
bread and went out with it.

00:02:35.177 --> 00:02:36.760 align:middle line:84%
He doesn't know where
we went with it.

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:40.480 align:middle line:90%
But we stole a wagon of bread.

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:42.340 align:middle line:90%
So he saw me.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:44.170 align:middle line:90%
He called me in.

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:47.890 align:middle line:84%
And he says to me, you know, I
have a real charge against you.

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:49.652 align:middle line:90%
I can arrest you right now.

00:02:49.652 --> 00:02:50.860 align:middle line:90%
I should arrest you, he says.

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:53.650 align:middle line:90%
You stole a wagon of bread.

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:56.030 align:middle line:84%
I says, no, I didn't
steal the bread.

00:02:56.030 --> 00:03:01.610 align:middle line:84%
We took it to the other
section to where our boys are,

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:03.960 align:middle line:84%
and they needed
hay for the horses.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:05.300 align:middle line:90%
He says, hay, I understand.

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:07.190 align:middle line:84%
But since when are the
horses eating bread?

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:10.730 align:middle line:84%
And bread in such
a big demand now.

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:12.420 align:middle line:90%
Then he says, don't lie to me.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:13.290 align:middle line:90%
Tell me the truth.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.440 align:middle line:90%
What did you do with the bread?

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:20.690 align:middle line:84%
So I says, well, we
took it into the ghetto.

00:03:20.690 --> 00:03:22.760 align:middle line:84%
There's some of our
people are hungry.

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:23.780 align:middle line:90%
We need bread.

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:27.560 align:middle line:84%
He said to me, I don't
want to hear about it.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:29.840 align:middle line:84%
And he says, and
the next time he

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:34.280 align:middle line:84%
says, if you want to do
something don't be a dumb Jew

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:35.855 align:middle line:90%
and let yourself being caught.

00:03:35.855 --> 00:03:38.720 align:middle line:90%


00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:39.770 align:middle line:90%
I saluted him.

00:03:39.770 --> 00:03:40.730 align:middle line:90%
And I said, yes sir.

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:42.800 align:middle line:84%
And turned around
and walked out.

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:45.750 align:middle line:84%
The next day we already
managed, we already found out.

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:47.455 align:middle line:84%
So he was actually
sympathetic towards--

00:03:47.455 --> 00:03:48.080 align:middle line:90%
He was helping.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:48.980 align:middle line:90%
He's trying to help.

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:49.550 align:middle line:90%
That was--

00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:54.800 align:middle line:84%
And then two days later, again,
we went in with one wagon.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:57.230 align:middle line:84%
And then he saw
me during the day.

00:03:57.230 --> 00:04:01.610 align:middle line:84%
And he calls me in, and says to
me, did you make your delivery?

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:02.840 align:middle line:90%
I said, yes sir.

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:05.180 align:middle line:90%
He says, job well done.

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:07.520 align:middle line:90%
And I went away.

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:10.850 align:middle line:84%
But things deteriorated
very badly.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:13.850 align:middle line:84%
Do you have any idea
this man's name?

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:17.180 align:middle line:84%
I haven't written down at home,
his son, I have the address.

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:18.410 align:middle line:90%
I have a letter from his son.

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:20.100 align:middle line:90%
I'm in contact with his son.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:20.930 align:middle line:90%
I have his picture.

00:04:20.930 --> 00:04:21.680 align:middle line:90%
I have everything.

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:22.610 align:middle line:90%
OK, let's go ahead.

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:31.370 align:middle line:84%
And things deteriorated in
the city, and out of town.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:34.310 align:middle line:90%
And the Hungarians didn't--

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:36.890 align:middle line:84%
the population
didn't like that we

00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:41.580 align:middle line:84%
as Jews who have been sitting
outside and sleeping outside,

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:44.120 align:middle line:84%
and instead of being
confined to the camp.

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:47.630 align:middle line:84%
So one day he came in
and arrested all of us,

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:50.497 align:middle line:90%
and threw us in the ghetto.

00:04:50.497 --> 00:04:52.080 align:middle line:84%
Well, they took you
out of the service

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:52.790 align:middle line:90%
then, and into the ghetto.

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:54.020 align:middle line:84%
And then throw it
into the ghetto.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:54.520 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:57.440 align:middle line:84%
We ran away from the
ghetto, back to the--

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:00.440 align:middle line:84%
again after three or four
days, there was no food.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:02.740 align:middle line:84%
Myself, there is
another guy here.

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:04.370 align:middle line:84%
He lives right
here in Cleveland.

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:05.750 align:middle line:90%
His name is Leonard Fox.

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:07.640 align:middle line:90%
He was with me at the time.

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:14.900 align:middle line:84%
We ran back in to the army,
took some breads in bags,

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:16.050 align:middle line:90%
as much as we could.

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:20.540 align:middle line:84%
I remember I had 14 loaves, and
I think he had the same amount.

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:23.390 align:middle line:84%
And we were caught
by bringing them in.

00:05:23.390 --> 00:05:28.610 align:middle line:90%
He got beaten up very badly.

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:30.380 align:middle line:90%
They gave him 45 lashes.

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:32.120 align:middle line:90%
He passed out.

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:36.110 align:middle line:84%
And by the time they got to me,
I somehow managed to run away,

00:05:36.110 --> 00:05:43.290 align:middle line:84%
jumped over, went away, and
I hid myself in the fields.

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:45.725 align:middle line:90%
And he didn't see me.

00:05:45.725 --> 00:05:48.630 align:middle line:84%
But came at night, I
didn't know what to do.

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:51.410 align:middle line:84%
I decided I better go
back in, in the ghetto.

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:53.333 align:middle line:84%
Because if I would
be on the street,

00:05:53.333 --> 00:05:55.750 align:middle line:84%
as the curfew is on the street,
the first thing they'll do

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:56.850 align:middle line:90%
is shoot me.

00:05:56.850 --> 00:05:57.350 align:middle line:90%
Sure.

00:05:57.350 --> 00:05:59.150 align:middle line:84%
So I didn't want
to take a chance.

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:02.430 align:middle line:84%
I thought my chances of
survival are better there.

00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:04.080 align:middle line:84%
So I went back
in, in the ghetto.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:05.460 align:middle line:90%
And that was my mistake.

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:07.440 align:middle line:84%
Without knowing,
the next morning,

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:10.670 align:middle line:84%
we were all rounded
up, put on the train,

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:12.590 align:middle line:90%
and away we went to Auschwitz.

00:06:12.590 --> 00:06:15.450 align:middle line:84%
Everybody in the ghetto, or
just you who were involved?

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:15.950 align:middle line:90%
Everybody.

00:06:15.950 --> 00:06:17.325 align:middle line:84%
The whole ghetto
was cleared out?

00:06:17.325 --> 00:06:18.700 align:middle line:84%
The entire ghetto
was liquidated.

00:06:18.700 --> 00:06:19.200 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:19.730 align:middle line:90%
I see.

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:23.000 align:middle line:84%
The entire ghetto was
liquidated, put in, in trains,

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:24.783 align:middle line:90%
and off we went to Auschwitz.

00:06:24.783 --> 00:06:25.700 align:middle line:90%
You went to Auschwitz.

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:26.660 align:middle line:90%
Now, all right.

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:32.000 align:middle line:84%
Now can you tell me, what were
your experiences in Auschwitz?

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:33.440 align:middle line:90%
Were you with your family?

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:33.980 align:middle line:90%
No.

00:06:33.980 --> 00:06:35.088 align:middle line:90%
I have heard--

00:06:35.088 --> 00:06:35.630 align:middle line:90%
That's right.

00:06:35.630 --> 00:06:36.950 align:middle line:90%
You were-- I had forgotten.

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:39.330 align:middle line:84%
I haven't heard
anything from my family.

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:42.520 align:middle line:84%
I don't know anything what's
happening with my hometown.

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:43.020 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:45.120 align:middle line:84%
The only thing we
heard is the rumors

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:47.190 align:middle line:90%
they have all been taken away.

00:06:47.190 --> 00:06:48.810 align:middle line:90%
We don't where.

00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:50.190 align:middle line:90%
Sure.

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:55.440 align:middle line:84%
Do you remember how long this
train ride was from the town

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:58.200 align:middle line:84%
where the army camp was
that ghetto, to Auschwitz?

00:06:58.200 --> 00:06:59.610 align:middle line:90%
How long were you on that train?

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:05.760 align:middle line:84%
Well, the ride took
us about five days.

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:08.700 align:middle line:84%
We used to stop
once or maybe twice,

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:11.430 align:middle line:90%
and receiving some water.

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:13.740 align:middle line:84%
We are not permitted
to get out of it.

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:19.620 align:middle line:84%
Just one guy may be jumping
out and filling dishes with

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:23.737 align:middle line:84%
and passing him water,
no food, just water.

00:07:23.737 --> 00:07:24.570 align:middle line:90%
No food, whatsoever.

00:07:24.570 --> 00:07:26.850 align:middle line:84%
Was this-- were
these regular trains?

00:07:26.850 --> 00:07:28.140 align:middle line:90%
Were these cattle trains?

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:28.980 align:middle line:90%
What kind of trains?

00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:29.480 align:middle line:90%
No.

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:31.110 align:middle line:90%
It was-- let me explain.

00:07:31.110 --> 00:07:35.100 align:middle line:84%
It was a train
with cattle wagons.

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:40.182 align:middle line:84%
In other words, they were
like boarded in all around.

00:07:40.182 --> 00:07:41.640 align:middle line:84%
But it wasn't the
passenger trains?

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:42.960 align:middle line:90%
No, no passenger trains.

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:44.015 align:middle line:90%
No, no, no.

00:07:44.015 --> 00:07:46.110 align:middle line:90%
It was commercial.

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:47.068 align:middle line:90%
They were freight cars.

00:07:47.068 --> 00:07:47.610 align:middle line:90%
Freight cars.

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:48.240 align:middle line:90%
Freight cars.

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:51.450 align:middle line:84%
Absolutely, freight
cars like you pushed in,

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:56.010 align:middle line:84%
80 to 100 people in one sitting
one on top on the other one.

00:07:56.010 --> 00:07:57.360 align:middle line:90%
They came the families.

00:07:57.360 --> 00:07:58.990 align:middle line:84%
They let the
families be together.

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:01.020 align:middle line:84%
But since I had no
family, nobody with me,

00:08:01.020 --> 00:08:05.340 align:middle line:84%
so we so to speak, the whole
hardcore guys were together

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:07.420 align:middle line:90%
again, half of it anyhow.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:10.860 align:middle line:84%
And we went, stick
together, and we went.

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:12.660 align:middle line:84%
That's the way we
arrived to Auschwitz.

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:13.160 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:17.070 align:middle line:84%
The screams, the
cries, the pushing,

00:08:17.070 --> 00:08:20.760 align:middle line:84%
the shoving in the
train those five days,

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:25.090 align:middle line:84%
I don't know if there is any
human being can describe them.

00:08:25.090 --> 00:08:25.590 align:middle line:90%
Terrible.

00:08:25.590 --> 00:08:31.470 align:middle line:84%
The cry from the kids, the
smell from older people

00:08:31.470 --> 00:08:33.220 align:middle line:90%
and from young children.

00:08:33.220 --> 00:08:34.679 align:middle line:90%
And you name it.

00:08:34.679 --> 00:08:36.091 align:middle line:90%
And it's hard.

00:08:36.091 --> 00:08:38.549 align:middle line:84%
I don't think there is anything
to describe it, just to say

00:08:38.549 --> 00:08:40.103 align:middle line:90%
it's terrible is not a word.

00:08:40.103 --> 00:08:42.270 align:middle line:84%
I don't think there is a
word in the dictionary that

00:08:42.270 --> 00:08:43.470 align:middle line:90%
would fit the description.

00:08:43.470 --> 00:08:46.590 align:middle line:84%
What was your
experience in Auschwitz?

00:08:46.590 --> 00:08:49.440 align:middle line:84%
Now, we are arriving
to Auschwitz.

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:54.780 align:middle line:84%
And there, the minute the
train pulled in and stopped,

00:08:54.780 --> 00:09:00.420 align:middle line:84%
it's like there would
be a complete new world.

00:09:00.420 --> 00:09:02.370 align:middle line:84%
Like you would
fall to the bottom,

00:09:02.370 --> 00:09:07.290 align:middle line:84%
will fall out of everything,
screams, the doors opened.

00:09:07.290 --> 00:09:10.200 align:middle line:90%
Do you recall the date?

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:19.180 align:middle line:84%
The date it was, two
days before, Shavuot.

00:09:19.180 --> 00:09:19.680 align:middle line:90%
Let's see.

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:20.700 align:middle line:90%
That would be--

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:21.570 align:middle line:90%
In May.

00:09:21.570 --> 00:09:29.050 align:middle line:84%
That would be in around
the 26th of May, 1943.

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:33.240 align:middle line:84%
This was when you were taken
from the ghetto and put in.

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:36.370 align:middle line:84%
And within that five day period
are your arrival in Auschwitz.

00:09:36.370 --> 00:09:36.870 align:middle line:90%
Yes, right.

00:09:36.870 --> 00:09:37.370 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:09:37.370 --> 00:09:40.300 align:middle line:84%
Describe your
arrival in the camp.

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:48.500 align:middle line:84%
In the camp, like I said
before, like it's a new plant.

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:52.360 align:middle line:84%
They opened up the doors,
the screaming, raus!

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:58.060 align:middle line:84%
The barking of the dogs,
and jumping the dogs,

00:09:58.060 --> 00:10:01.060 align:middle line:84%
the SS holding back,
they jump-- the dog

00:10:01.060 --> 00:10:02.630 align:middle line:90%
from jumping on anybody.

00:10:02.630 --> 00:10:06.340 align:middle line:84%
And those big sticks
and black uniforms

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:10.120 align:middle line:84%
with a Totenkopf, the
death hats on their--

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:15.430 align:middle line:90%
it is impossible to describe.

00:10:15.430 --> 00:10:19.310 align:middle line:84%
And the screamings, and the
pushing, and the shoving, raus!

00:10:19.310 --> 00:10:22.150 align:middle line:84%
Eintreten, raus,
eintreten, which means out.

00:10:22.150 --> 00:10:25.720 align:middle line:84%
In line, out, get in
line, out, get in line.

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:26.920 align:middle line:90%
That's all.

00:10:26.920 --> 00:10:31.060 align:middle line:84%
And then kids lost--
babies lost their mothers.

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:34.570 align:middle line:84%
Mothers lost their husbands,
and fathers lost their children,

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:35.680 align:middle line:90%
and screaming.

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:37.630 align:middle line:90%
Everybody looking for everybody.

00:10:37.630 --> 00:10:39.820 align:middle line:90%
And the dogs barking.

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:43.820 align:middle line:84%
Finally everybody found
everybody, got in line.

00:10:43.820 --> 00:10:45.500 align:middle line:90%
Now, we are walking.

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:50.390 align:middle line:84%
They separate men on one
side, women and children

00:10:50.390 --> 00:10:51.650 align:middle line:90%
on the other side.

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:55.490 align:middle line:84%
Nobody in his wildest
dreams would ever

00:10:55.490 --> 00:10:57.410 align:middle line:84%
imagined that this
is the last time

00:10:57.410 --> 00:10:59.234 align:middle line:90%
that they will see each other.

00:10:59.234 --> 00:11:01.010 align:middle line:90%
Sure.

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:07.820 align:middle line:84%
Now as we got in line,
put us in a line,

00:11:07.820 --> 00:11:09.710 align:middle line:90%
men separated, women separated.

00:11:09.710 --> 00:11:11.990 align:middle line:84%
This has to be a terrible
feel-- you had no idea what

00:11:11.990 --> 00:11:13.590 align:middle line:90%
the future held for you.

00:11:13.590 --> 00:11:14.510 align:middle line:90%
We don't see nothing.

00:11:14.510 --> 00:11:14.750 align:middle line:90%
We don't--

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:15.833 align:middle line:90%
You're told you're going--

00:11:15.833 --> 00:11:20.390 align:middle line:84%
You are so preoccupied with
the events at the moment

00:11:20.390 --> 00:11:22.550 align:middle line:84%
that your mind doesn't
even wander away.

00:11:22.550 --> 00:11:23.550 align:middle line:90%
Your mind is right here.

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:25.175 align:middle line:84%
But of course, it's
a question for what

00:11:25.175 --> 00:11:26.300 align:middle line:90%
is the next moment coming.

00:11:26.300 --> 00:11:28.042 align:middle line:84%
When you were put on
that train, did you

00:11:28.042 --> 00:11:29.125 align:middle line:90%
know where you were going?

00:11:29.125 --> 00:11:30.320 align:middle line:90%
No, no idea.

00:11:30.320 --> 00:11:30.900 align:middle line:90%
No idea.

00:11:30.900 --> 00:11:31.400 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:11:31.400 --> 00:11:32.273 align:middle line:90%
No idea.

00:11:32.273 --> 00:11:34.190 align:middle line:84%
And when you stopped and
you saw the soldiers,

00:11:34.190 --> 00:11:35.180 align:middle line:90%
we don't where we are.

00:11:35.180 --> 00:11:36.770 align:middle line:84%
You don't know what's going
to happen to you from one

00:11:36.770 --> 00:11:38.030 align:middle line:90%
moment to the next.

00:11:38.030 --> 00:11:39.440 align:middle line:90%
We don't know where we are.

00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:41.270 align:middle line:90%
We don't know what's happening.

00:11:41.270 --> 00:11:44.990 align:middle line:84%
The minds-- excuse me--
are so occupied just

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:47.130 align:middle line:90%
to be from the moment.

00:11:47.130 --> 00:11:48.890 align:middle line:90%
Sure.

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:52.430 align:middle line:84%
Finally, we are in a line,
and we start walking.

00:11:52.430 --> 00:11:57.860 align:middle line:84%
And there we see three
SS, all beautiful dressed,

00:11:57.860 --> 00:12:02.810 align:middle line:84%
fancy clothes, shiny
boots, like a mirror.

00:12:02.810 --> 00:12:05.940 align:middle line:84%
Later, we find out
it was Dr. Mengele.

00:12:05.940 --> 00:12:10.490 align:middle line:84%
And he's standing there
and like this, you walk up.

00:12:10.490 --> 00:12:13.000 align:middle line:84%
And you're supposed
to tell them your age.

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:17.530 align:middle line:84%
You come to him and you say
16, 17, 18, whatever, 50, 20,

00:12:17.530 --> 00:12:18.655 align:middle line:90%
whatever your age is.

00:12:18.655 --> 00:12:19.300 align:middle line:90%
Sure.

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:20.470 align:middle line:90%
I came in front of him.

00:12:20.470 --> 00:12:21.620 align:middle line:90%
I said, 17.

00:12:21.620 --> 00:12:24.236 align:middle line:90%
[NON-ENGLISH] 17.

00:12:24.236 --> 00:12:26.710 align:middle line:84%
He looked at me and
makes like this,

00:12:26.710 --> 00:12:29.410 align:middle line:90%
means I'm going to the right.

00:12:29.410 --> 00:12:32.740 align:middle line:84%
Other guys, to the right,
to the right, to the right.

00:12:32.740 --> 00:12:33.925 align:middle line:90%
Then he makes like this.

00:12:33.925 --> 00:12:35.590 align:middle line:90%
It means to the left.

00:12:35.590 --> 00:12:37.617 align:middle line:84%
We didn't know the meaning
of it, what it means.

00:12:37.617 --> 00:12:38.200 align:middle line:90%
Of course not.

00:12:38.200 --> 00:12:42.350 align:middle line:84%
Left and what it
means to the right.

00:12:42.350 --> 00:12:46.810 align:middle line:84%
And finally it's over,
so to speak, that--

00:12:46.810 --> 00:12:47.360 align:middle line:90%
Selection.

00:12:47.360 --> 00:12:48.340 align:middle line:90%
--selection.

00:12:48.340 --> 00:12:49.480 align:middle line:90%
We got in.

00:12:49.480 --> 00:12:53.200 align:middle line:84%
And now we are lined up
men, only men, no woman,

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:53.960 align:middle line:90%
no children.

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:56.650 align:middle line:84%
They are all separated
in a different direction.

00:12:56.650 --> 00:13:01.300 align:middle line:84%
We are lined up eight
in a line, and a whole

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:05.680 align:middle line:84%
on the back, a whole line, I
don't know how many thousands.

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:07.270 align:middle line:90%
And I'm in the middle.

00:13:07.270 --> 00:13:09.950 align:middle line:90%
And we are about to walk.

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:14.120 align:middle line:84%
From far, I can see there is
a big sign through a gate.

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:16.760 align:middle line:84%
And it says, Arbeit
macht frei, which

00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:20.030 align:middle line:90%
means work brings liberty.

00:13:20.030 --> 00:13:25.920 align:middle line:84%
So to go through
that gate, as we

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:29.460 align:middle line:84%
are walking towards the gate,
on both sides are barracks.

00:13:29.460 --> 00:13:32.340 align:middle line:84%
Are you carrying
anything, any possessions?

00:13:32.340 --> 00:13:33.690 align:middle line:90%
I just have one--

00:13:33.690 --> 00:13:36.720 align:middle line:90%
on my back, I have a sack with--

00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:38.040 align:middle line:90%
A rucksack, a knapsack.

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:39.660 align:middle line:84%
Yeah, right, a
knapsack, with some,

00:13:39.660 --> 00:13:43.360 align:middle line:84%
a few of my personal
belongings, nothing else.

00:13:43.360 --> 00:13:49.050 align:middle line:84%
And as we are walking,
somehow I had the feeling

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:54.850 align:middle line:84%
that somebody is looking at me
and that something will happen.

00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:56.970 align:middle line:84%
I looked around, and
I didn't see nobody.

00:13:56.970 --> 00:14:01.800 align:middle line:84%
But I saw one SS man, soldier
walking with a big stick

00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:04.830 align:middle line:90%
and with a whip in his hand.

00:14:04.830 --> 00:14:10.080 align:middle line:84%
And I saw him walking,
more I came closer to him,

00:14:10.080 --> 00:14:12.540 align:middle line:84%
and closer he came
to me, somehow

00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:17.610 align:middle line:84%
something in me starting
to work harder and harder.

00:14:17.610 --> 00:14:19.020 align:middle line:90%
And from out of the blue sky--

00:14:19.020 --> 00:14:19.710 align:middle line:90%
It was fear.

00:14:19.710 --> 00:14:20.430 align:middle line:90%
It was fear.

00:14:20.430 --> 00:14:23.640 align:middle line:84%
No, it was-- I can't
describe the feeling,

00:14:23.640 --> 00:14:25.290 align:middle line:90%
and it was something.

00:14:25.290 --> 00:14:29.000 align:middle line:84%
No fear, I wasn't afraid
of anything in those days.

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:31.080 align:middle line:84%
Sure, you were a young
healthy, young man.

00:14:31.080 --> 00:14:31.863 align:middle line:90%
It's something--

00:14:31.863 --> 00:14:33.030 align:middle line:90%
Something's going to happen.

00:14:33.030 --> 00:14:36.210 align:middle line:84%
Something special--
something is about to happen.

00:14:36.210 --> 00:14:38.350 align:middle line:90%
And he came over closer to me.

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:41.100 align:middle line:84%
And as soon as he came a
few steps away from me,

00:14:41.100 --> 00:14:45.240 align:middle line:84%
our eyes met, and he
had a whip in his hand.

00:14:45.240 --> 00:14:48.330 align:middle line:84%
And he started to hit
me, saying [NON-ENGLISH]..

00:14:48.330 --> 00:14:51.257 align:middle line:90%


00:14:51.257 --> 00:14:52.090 align:middle line:90%
What does that mean?

00:14:52.090 --> 00:14:57.300 align:middle line:84%
It means the damn dark, move,
that you further comes away

00:14:57.300 --> 00:15:01.560 align:middle line:84%
from here, disappear,
go, hit me a few times.

00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:07.110 align:middle line:84%
And I was just about ready
to drop my rucksack, the bag,

00:15:07.110 --> 00:15:09.270 align:middle line:90%
and just ready to jump on him.

00:15:09.270 --> 00:15:12.090 align:middle line:84%
When one of my friends in
the back, grabbed me and says

00:15:12.090 --> 00:15:13.470 align:middle line:90%
don't get crazy.

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:16.420 align:middle line:90%
Not now.

00:15:16.420 --> 00:15:18.250 align:middle line:90%
Another time now.

00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:20.230 align:middle line:90%
He hold me back and we walked.

00:15:20.230 --> 00:15:22.750 align:middle line:90%
And this is happening so fast.

00:15:22.750 --> 00:15:25.520 align:middle line:84%
And I have to keep
on walking in line.

00:15:25.520 --> 00:15:31.320 align:middle line:84%
And as I am walking, a
thought came to me, why me?

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:32.230 align:middle line:90%
Sure.

00:15:32.230 --> 00:15:35.290 align:middle line:84%
Here I am, I'm
walking in a line.

00:15:35.290 --> 00:15:36.805 align:middle line:90%
With so many.

00:15:36.805 --> 00:15:39.490 align:middle line:84%
So many people and
that particular feeling

00:15:39.490 --> 00:15:42.518 align:middle line:84%
after me, if he had come
in line, hit this guy,

00:15:42.518 --> 00:15:43.060 align:middle line:90%
hit that guy.

00:15:43.060 --> 00:15:43.852 align:middle line:90%
Yeah, hit this Jew.

00:15:43.852 --> 00:15:46.720 align:middle line:90%
So hit me too, so tough luck.

00:15:46.720 --> 00:15:50.020 align:middle line:90%
But why hit me?

00:15:50.020 --> 00:15:52.510 align:middle line:84%
And I just turned
around automatically,

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:56.620 align:middle line:84%
and I was just passing the
gate to going into the camp.

00:15:56.620 --> 00:16:01.120 align:middle line:84%
It's just from walking I was
just about passing the gate,

00:16:01.120 --> 00:16:03.970 align:middle line:84%
I looked around and
I said, no matter

00:16:03.970 --> 00:16:09.640 align:middle line:84%
what you SOBs will do to me, I
will survive, no matter what.

00:16:09.640 --> 00:16:13.300 align:middle line:84%
And something
overcame me and kept

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:18.620 align:middle line:84%
me going through all my troubles
I had for the rest of my life,

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:19.400 align:middle line:90%
till this day.

00:16:19.400 --> 00:16:21.060 align:middle line:90%
It's something in me.

00:16:21.060 --> 00:16:21.560 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:16:21.560 --> 00:16:22.775 align:middle line:90%
There's something that I--

00:16:22.775 --> 00:16:24.170 align:middle line:90%
I don't know what it is.

00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:25.490 align:middle line:90%
Isn't that something?

00:16:25.490 --> 00:16:29.840 align:middle line:84%
And that helped me
further, you'll see.

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:31.040 align:middle line:90%
So here we are.

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:33.770 align:middle line:90%
We are in the camp.

00:16:33.770 --> 00:16:36.590 align:middle line:84%
The first thing we come in,
of course, the hollering,

00:16:36.590 --> 00:16:38.480 align:middle line:90%
the pushing, the shoving.

00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:39.740 align:middle line:90%
You know, and all of that.

00:16:39.740 --> 00:16:41.990 align:middle line:90%
It's undescribable.

00:16:41.990 --> 00:16:43.910 align:middle line:90%
And then we see this guy.

00:16:43.910 --> 00:16:45.440 align:middle line:90%
And I say, hey.

00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:46.580 align:middle line:90%
I am here.

00:16:46.580 --> 00:16:49.200 align:middle line:84%
I just arrived
yesterday, the other day.

00:16:49.200 --> 00:16:53.540 align:middle line:90%
Guys from different towns.

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:54.530 align:middle line:90%
Where is my sister?

00:16:54.530 --> 00:16:55.730 align:middle line:90%
Your sister arrived.

00:16:55.730 --> 00:16:56.360 align:middle line:90%
She is there.

00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:59.450 align:middle line:84%
We have seen her last night
on the other side of the wire,

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:00.380 align:middle line:90%
that kind of stuff.

00:17:00.380 --> 00:17:01.460 align:middle line:90%
Right, right.

00:17:01.460 --> 00:17:02.180 align:middle line:90%
And here we are.

00:17:02.180 --> 00:17:03.740 align:middle line:90%
Did you find any friends?

00:17:03.740 --> 00:17:06.020 align:middle line:90%
Oh, yes, I had the group of my--

00:17:06.020 --> 00:17:08.089 align:middle line:84%
Well, I met other,
but not from home yet?

00:17:08.089 --> 00:17:08.660 align:middle line:90%
Oh, yes.

00:17:08.660 --> 00:17:11.220 align:middle line:84%
I'll-- I haven't
found anything yet.

00:17:11.220 --> 00:17:13.490 align:middle line:90%
I'm still in, in my own clothes.

00:17:13.490 --> 00:17:14.750 align:middle line:90%
Finally, we walk in.

00:17:14.750 --> 00:17:16.490 align:middle line:90%
We go in to take a shower.

00:17:16.490 --> 00:17:18.770 align:middle line:84%
So we're going to
bathe, to take a shower,

00:17:18.770 --> 00:17:21.660 align:middle line:84%
take off everything, and
leave it on this side.

00:17:21.660 --> 00:17:25.375 align:middle line:84%
And they say to us when you come
out, you'll pick it back up.

00:17:25.375 --> 00:17:26.750 align:middle line:84%
We know damn well
that we are not

00:17:26.750 --> 00:17:28.730 align:middle line:84%
going to come out
on this side again,

00:17:28.730 --> 00:17:31.370 align:middle line:84%
that everything what we leave
here is going to be left.

00:17:31.370 --> 00:17:33.440 align:middle line:90%
Sure.

00:17:33.440 --> 00:17:36.420 align:middle line:84%
So anyway, we left
everything here.

00:17:36.420 --> 00:17:38.780 align:middle line:90%
We went out on the other side.

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:42.650 align:middle line:84%
The only thing we were
allowed to take is the shoes.

00:17:42.650 --> 00:17:44.150 align:middle line:90%
Everything was left.

00:17:44.150 --> 00:17:45.650 align:middle line:90%
We went out on the other side.

00:17:45.650 --> 00:17:49.670 align:middle line:84%
They gave us a shirt,
a pair of underwear,

00:17:49.670 --> 00:17:53.480 align:middle line:84%
and a pair of those
prison clothings.

00:17:53.480 --> 00:17:54.020 align:middle line:90%
Yes, right.

00:17:54.020 --> 00:17:57.350 align:middle line:84%
And you had your own
shoes, snow shoes.

00:17:57.350 --> 00:18:00.710 align:middle line:84%
Got dressed, they took us
out in front of a barrack.

00:18:00.710 --> 00:18:04.190 align:middle line:84%
That's the first time we
learned the real McCoy, what's--

00:18:04.190 --> 00:18:05.270 align:middle line:90%
That you're prisoners.

00:18:05.270 --> 00:18:08.270 align:middle line:90%
That what we are and what it is.

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:10.580 align:middle line:84%
Right away, they
gave us a number.

00:18:10.580 --> 00:18:14.900 align:middle line:84%
They cut our hair,
everywhere, everything.

00:18:14.900 --> 00:18:16.040 align:middle line:90%
They gave us a number.

00:18:16.040 --> 00:18:18.555 align:middle line:90%
From now on, 8485.

00:18:18.555 --> 00:18:19.430 align:middle line:90%
That was your number.

00:18:19.430 --> 00:18:20.810 align:middle line:90%
That's my number.

00:18:20.810 --> 00:18:24.080 align:middle line:90%
And you don't call you by name.

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:26.930 align:middle line:90%
They only call the number 8485.

00:18:26.930 --> 00:18:28.730 align:middle line:90%
And you say, here.

00:18:28.730 --> 00:18:29.840 align:middle line:90%
You know, and all that.

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:31.890 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:18:31.890 --> 00:18:36.175 align:middle line:84%
They bring us, give us
everybody, we got a--

00:18:36.175 --> 00:18:38.040 align:middle line:90%
I don't know how to call it.

00:18:38.040 --> 00:18:39.600 align:middle line:90%
We called it a shissel.

00:18:39.600 --> 00:18:41.700 align:middle line:90%
A canteen, a little pot.

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:43.140 align:middle line:90%
It's not a canteen.

00:18:43.140 --> 00:18:44.260 align:middle line:90%
It's a pot.

00:18:44.260 --> 00:18:44.760 align:middle line:90%
Yeah.

00:18:44.760 --> 00:18:46.590 align:middle line:90%
Yeah, I mean a little tin dish.

00:18:46.590 --> 00:18:47.190 align:middle line:90%
Tin dish.

00:18:47.190 --> 00:18:49.020 align:middle line:90%
So that you-- to eat from.

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:51.490 align:middle line:90%
They threw in some stuff in it.

00:18:51.490 --> 00:18:53.840 align:middle line:90%
Nobody could ever have eaten it.

00:18:53.840 --> 00:18:54.810 align:middle line:90%
Nobody, nobody.

00:18:54.810 --> 00:18:55.380 align:middle line:90%
Terrible.

00:18:55.380 --> 00:18:58.110 align:middle line:90%
No taste, no, we threw it away.

00:18:58.110 --> 00:19:00.060 align:middle line:90%
After three days, he got hungry.

00:19:00.060 --> 00:19:01.060 align:middle line:90%
He got used to it.

00:19:01.060 --> 00:19:01.720 align:middle line:90%
And we had to drink it.

00:19:01.720 --> 00:19:02.220 align:middle line:90%
Sure.

00:19:02.220 --> 00:19:05.115 align:middle line:84%
So, we used to get
that stuff once a day.

00:19:05.115 --> 00:19:08.190 align:middle line:90%


00:19:08.190 --> 00:19:12.210 align:middle line:84%
Bitter water, it looked
like tea in the morning,

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:13.680 align:middle line:90%
nothing with it.

00:19:13.680 --> 00:19:17.790 align:middle line:84%
In the evening, we used to
get a ration of bread, which

00:19:17.790 --> 00:19:22.080 align:middle line:84%
is take a pound bread,
divided in four,

00:19:22.080 --> 00:19:25.980 align:middle line:84%
you get one rash, two
slices of margarine,

00:19:25.980 --> 00:19:28.110 align:middle line:90%
and one slice of slice of jelly.

00:19:28.110 --> 00:19:29.610 align:middle line:90%
That was our daily--

00:19:29.610 --> 00:19:30.390 align:middle line:90%
Your daily ration.

00:19:30.390 --> 00:19:31.650 align:middle line:90%
--ration.

00:19:31.650 --> 00:19:33.400 align:middle line:90%
And we had to live on this.

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:35.070 align:middle line:90%
So we have been sitting outside.

00:19:35.070 --> 00:19:37.900 align:middle line:84%
We didn't know
what's going on what.

00:19:37.900 --> 00:19:41.940 align:middle line:84%
Second day, somebody says to
me that in the next barrack

00:19:41.940 --> 00:19:45.030 align:middle line:90%
there are boys from my hometown.

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:46.737 align:middle line:90%
I went to see them.

00:19:46.737 --> 00:19:48.820 align:middle line:84%
And sure enough, there
were boys from my hometown.

00:19:48.820 --> 00:19:52.320 align:middle line:90%
And they all say, Larry.

00:19:52.320 --> 00:19:54.930 align:middle line:90%
Your dad left yesterday.

00:19:54.930 --> 00:19:56.340 align:middle line:90%
Where did he leave to?

00:19:56.340 --> 00:19:58.830 align:middle line:90%
A transport went to Warsaw.

00:19:58.830 --> 00:20:01.230 align:middle line:90%
And he is in Warsaw.

00:20:01.230 --> 00:20:05.080 align:middle line:84%
This is already after the
liquidation of the ghetto.

00:20:05.080 --> 00:20:07.350 align:middle line:90%
It's already 1944.

00:20:07.350 --> 00:20:09.510 align:middle line:84%
And this is after the
liquidation of the--

00:20:09.510 --> 00:20:10.093 align:middle line:90%
Of the Warsaw.

00:20:10.093 --> 00:20:12.260 align:middle line:84%
The Warsaw-- and in '43,
they liquidated the ghetto,

00:20:12.260 --> 00:20:14.940 align:middle line:84%
and after the liquidation of the
ghetto, he was taken to Warsaw.

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:17.040 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:20:17.040 --> 00:20:19.050 align:middle line:90%
I says, who else is there?

00:20:19.050 --> 00:20:20.640 align:middle line:90%
They says, your uncle was there.

00:20:20.640 --> 00:20:23.970 align:middle line:84%
And this friend, and this
friend, and his father, and all

00:20:23.970 --> 00:20:26.220 align:middle line:90%
of that.

00:20:26.220 --> 00:20:26.910 align:middle line:90%
All right.

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:28.600 align:middle line:90%
I don't know anything.

00:20:28.600 --> 00:20:31.320 align:middle line:90%
They are going to Warsaw.

00:20:31.320 --> 00:20:35.027 align:middle line:84%
The next day, they pass
us by, no nothing happens.

00:20:35.027 --> 00:20:36.110 align:middle line:90%
You're not doing anything.

00:20:36.110 --> 00:20:37.240 align:middle line:90%
You have no routine yet?

00:20:37.240 --> 00:20:37.390 align:middle line:90%
No, nothing.

00:20:37.390 --> 00:20:38.515 align:middle line:90%
You're just sitting around.

00:20:38.515 --> 00:20:41.050 align:middle line:84%
Sitting around, and
you know, nothing,

00:20:41.050 --> 00:20:43.530 align:middle line:84%
talking what's going
to be, where do we go.

00:20:43.530 --> 00:20:48.550 align:middle line:84%
And in the meantime, we have
a smell, we feel a smell.

00:20:48.550 --> 00:20:50.620 align:middle line:84%
And we don't know
what the smell is.

00:20:50.620 --> 00:20:51.580 align:middle line:90%
Then we learn.

00:20:51.580 --> 00:20:52.893 align:middle line:90%
They showed us the chimneys.

00:20:52.893 --> 00:20:55.310 align:middle line:84%
They said, this is your parents
going through the chimney.

00:20:55.310 --> 00:20:56.740 align:middle line:90%
This is the crematorium there.

00:20:56.740 --> 00:20:58.210 align:middle line:90%
This is the smell.

00:20:58.210 --> 00:20:59.495 align:middle line:90%
And we thought, eh.

00:20:59.495 --> 00:21:00.370 align:middle line:90%
We didn't believe it.

00:21:00.370 --> 00:21:02.210 align:middle line:84%
Couldn't be, nobody
could be so inhuman.

00:21:02.210 --> 00:21:02.710 align:middle line:90%
Yeah.

00:21:02.710 --> 00:21:06.065 align:middle line:84%
That's [NON-ENGLISH] who was
going to do something like

00:21:06.065 --> 00:21:06.565 align:middle line:90%
that.

00:21:06.565 --> 00:21:09.370 align:middle line:90%


00:21:09.370 --> 00:21:12.390 align:middle line:84%
But one thing everybody said,
get out of Auschwitz as fast

00:21:12.390 --> 00:21:14.670 align:middle line:90%
as you can.

00:21:14.670 --> 00:21:17.820 align:middle line:84%
The third day, I
again met another boy.

00:21:17.820 --> 00:21:19.170 align:middle line:90%
He tells me the same story.

00:21:19.170 --> 00:21:21.390 align:middle line:84%
My father was here and he
left with the transport.

00:21:21.390 --> 00:21:23.850 align:middle line:90%
He went to Warsaw.

00:21:23.850 --> 00:21:26.040 align:middle line:84%
In the evening, rumors
started to spread

00:21:26.040 --> 00:21:29.640 align:middle line:84%
that tomorrow morning there is
a transport going to Warsaw.

00:21:29.640 --> 00:21:31.920 align:middle line:84%
And it's going to be
from a different block,

00:21:31.920 --> 00:21:34.900 align:middle line:84%
not where I am, but
the other block.

00:21:34.900 --> 00:21:36.690 align:middle line:90%
So I went over.

00:21:36.690 --> 00:21:40.860 align:middle line:84%
And I found somebody who had
a friend in the other block.

00:21:40.860 --> 00:21:42.780 align:middle line:90%
Names didn't mean anything.

00:21:42.780 --> 00:21:44.470 align:middle line:90%
Numbers didn't mean anything.

00:21:44.470 --> 00:21:45.900 align:middle line:84%
It's just the
numbers, the count.

00:21:45.900 --> 00:21:47.790 align:middle line:84%
In other words, if
you counted 50 people,

00:21:47.790 --> 00:21:49.230 align:middle line:90%
you had to have 50 people.

00:21:49.230 --> 00:21:50.550 align:middle line:90%
That's all what counted.

00:21:50.550 --> 00:21:52.020 align:middle line:90%
The rest didn't mean anything.

00:21:52.020 --> 00:21:56.520 align:middle line:84%
So we changed He came over
here, and I went over there.

00:21:56.520 --> 00:21:59.770 align:middle line:84%
And to make the
long story short,

00:21:59.770 --> 00:22:03.450 align:middle line:84%
the next day, sure enough, got
up in the morning to appell.

00:22:03.450 --> 00:22:08.650 align:middle line:84%
Eintreten, and, so a day
later, 24 hours later, I

00:22:08.650 --> 00:22:09.610 align:middle line:90%
was in Warsaw.

00:22:09.610 --> 00:22:12.970 align:middle line:84%
And sure enough,
there was my father.

00:22:12.970 --> 00:22:14.830 align:middle line:84%
Why were they sending
you to Warsaw?

00:22:14.830 --> 00:22:17.710 align:middle line:84%
To the same place,
to work where those,

00:22:17.710 --> 00:22:19.630 align:middle line:84%
the transport from
my father before.

00:22:19.630 --> 00:22:20.500 align:middle line:90%
Oh, I see.

00:22:20.500 --> 00:22:24.488 align:middle line:84%
Oh, so they sent you to a
work place, to work there.

00:22:24.488 --> 00:22:25.780 align:middle line:90%
Yes, to the same working force.

00:22:25.780 --> 00:22:26.280 align:middle line:90%
I see.

00:22:26.280 --> 00:22:27.370 align:middle line:90%
OK, I didn't realize.

00:22:27.370 --> 00:22:30.130 align:middle line:84%
So all right, so actually
then, you left Auschwitz.

00:22:30.130 --> 00:22:32.770 align:middle line:84%
You really weren't
there maybe a week.

00:22:32.770 --> 00:22:34.370 align:middle line:90%
Less, one day less than a week.

00:22:34.370 --> 00:22:34.870 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:22:34.870 --> 00:22:35.230 align:middle line:90%
One day less than a week.

00:22:35.230 --> 00:22:36.230 align:middle line:90%
Then you went to Warsaw.

00:22:36.230 --> 00:22:38.620 align:middle line:84%
We went on the same transport,
and they took us to--

00:22:38.620 --> 00:22:39.220 align:middle line:90%
I didn't know.

00:22:39.220 --> 00:22:40.030 align:middle line:90%
I took a gamble.

00:22:40.030 --> 00:22:41.410 align:middle line:90%
But he said, Warsaw, so I said.

00:22:41.410 --> 00:22:41.910 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:22:41.910 --> 00:22:43.330 align:middle line:90%
And it turned out, yeah.

00:22:43.330 --> 00:22:45.220 align:middle line:84%
As soon as I walked
in the camp, I already

00:22:45.220 --> 00:22:47.320 align:middle line:90%
recognized my hometown people.

00:22:47.320 --> 00:22:49.090 align:middle line:84%
OK, now what was the
name of this camp?

00:22:49.090 --> 00:22:50.020 align:middle line:90%
Was it a camp?

00:22:50.020 --> 00:22:50.770 align:middle line:90%
No, it was not.

00:22:50.770 --> 00:22:55.330 align:middle line:84%
It was like a camp, but
it was in the ghetto

00:22:55.330 --> 00:22:58.265 align:middle line:84%
where the Warsaw ghetto
was on the same place.

00:22:58.265 --> 00:22:58.765 align:middle line:90%
I see.

00:22:58.765 --> 00:23:00.348 align:middle line:84%
But it didn't have
a name or anything?

00:23:00.348 --> 00:23:00.910 align:middle line:90%
No, nothing.

00:23:00.910 --> 00:23:01.410 align:middle line:90%
Just--

00:23:01.410 --> 00:23:03.220 align:middle line:84%
So you saw people
from your town.

00:23:03.220 --> 00:23:05.020 align:middle line:84%
Just, and I saw people
from my hometown.

00:23:05.020 --> 00:23:07.427 align:middle line:84%
And they all started to
say your father is here.

00:23:07.427 --> 00:23:08.260 align:middle line:90%
Your father is here.

00:23:08.260 --> 00:23:08.830 align:middle line:90%
So I felt.

00:23:08.830 --> 00:23:09.160 align:middle line:90%
How wonderful.

00:23:09.160 --> 00:23:09.785 align:middle line:90%
I felt not bad.

00:23:09.785 --> 00:23:12.730 align:middle line:84%
Now how long had it been since
you had left your family?

00:23:12.730 --> 00:23:15.370 align:middle line:84%
I left my family, it was
six weeks, I haven't seen

00:23:15.370 --> 00:23:16.630 align:middle line:90%
and I haven't heard from them.

00:23:16.630 --> 00:23:19.250 align:middle line:84%
That's all the time it
was from the army to--

00:23:19.250 --> 00:23:19.750 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:23:19.750 --> 00:23:22.030 align:middle line:84%
From the time you left
home, it's only six weeks?

00:23:22.030 --> 00:23:22.530 align:middle line:90%
Yeah.

00:23:22.530 --> 00:23:24.220 align:middle line:84%
OK, I just wanted
to get a time--

00:23:24.220 --> 00:23:28.150 align:middle line:84%
Late April, same year,
till after Passover.

00:23:28.150 --> 00:23:29.140 align:middle line:90%
Right, I understand.

00:23:29.140 --> 00:23:29.640 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:23:29.640 --> 00:23:30.160 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:23:30.160 --> 00:23:32.675 align:middle line:90%
So here I am.

00:23:32.675 --> 00:23:35.050 align:middle line:84%
And we waited till after we
had to stay in line, after we

00:23:35.050 --> 00:23:35.830 align:middle line:90%
were dismissed.

00:23:35.830 --> 00:23:39.880 align:middle line:84%
I was with my father and, he
right away he starts crying.

00:23:39.880 --> 00:23:43.900 align:middle line:84%
And you know, and he says to
me the rumors about the kids.

00:23:43.900 --> 00:23:45.790 align:middle line:84%
And then he says,
ah, it's only rumors.

00:23:45.790 --> 00:23:48.250 align:middle line:84%
And he says, and on the
other hand, I know he says,

00:23:48.250 --> 00:23:50.800 align:middle line:84%
they're eating well and
they're drinking well.

00:23:50.800 --> 00:23:51.910 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:23:51.910 --> 00:23:54.880 align:middle line:84%
But I met another boy,
who the fact of the matter

00:23:54.880 --> 00:23:56.530 align:middle line:84%
is he is here in
Cleveland too, who is

00:23:56.530 --> 00:23:58.970 align:middle line:90%
a Polish boy, also in the camp.

00:23:58.970 --> 00:24:00.100 align:middle line:90%
I don't know where I am.

00:24:00.100 --> 00:24:01.210 align:middle line:90%
I only know it's Warsaw.

00:24:01.210 --> 00:24:04.600 align:middle line:84%
I don't know what it is, where
I am, except that Warsaw.

00:24:04.600 --> 00:24:07.120 align:middle line:90%
Excuse me for interrupting you.

00:24:07.120 --> 00:24:09.460 align:middle line:84%
Did your father,
when he was there,

00:24:09.460 --> 00:24:12.110 align:middle line:84%
did he know where his wife
and your sisters were?

00:24:12.110 --> 00:24:13.360 align:middle line:90%
Yeah, he didn't know anything.

00:24:13.360 --> 00:24:14.200 align:middle line:90%
They were in Auschwitz.

00:24:14.200 --> 00:24:15.040 align:middle line:90%
They are in Auschwitz.

00:24:15.040 --> 00:24:15.490 align:middle line:90%
That's all.

00:24:15.490 --> 00:24:15.910 align:middle line:90%
OK, that's all he knew.

00:24:15.910 --> 00:24:16.598 align:middle line:90%
And he-- yes.

00:24:16.598 --> 00:24:17.140 align:middle line:90%
And he said--

00:24:17.140 --> 00:24:18.910 align:middle line:84%
That's where they separated
the men from the women.

00:24:18.910 --> 00:24:19.180 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:24:19.180 --> 00:24:19.690 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:24:19.690 --> 00:24:21.580 align:middle line:84%
The events were the
regular process.

00:24:21.580 --> 00:24:25.150 align:middle line:84%
And he said that
somebody told them

00:24:25.150 --> 00:24:27.610 align:middle line:84%
in Auschwitz they are going
to get bread, white bread,

00:24:27.610 --> 00:24:29.410 align:middle line:90%
and they will live yet.

00:24:29.410 --> 00:24:32.570 align:middle line:84%
I mean live good, and
there was no problem.

00:24:32.570 --> 00:24:33.070 align:middle line:90%
All right.

00:24:33.070 --> 00:24:35.320 align:middle line:90%
And they will survive.

00:24:35.320 --> 00:24:36.640 align:middle line:90%
It's just a matter of time.

00:24:36.640 --> 00:24:38.350 align:middle line:90%
Yeah.

00:24:38.350 --> 00:24:42.085 align:middle line:84%
I already knew the
truth, but I didn't

00:24:42.085 --> 00:24:43.210 align:middle line:90%
want it to hamper with him.

00:24:43.210 --> 00:24:46.240 align:middle line:84%
I didn't want to take away his
hopes, and to make them misery.

00:24:46.240 --> 00:24:48.700 align:middle line:84%
And I thought to myself, as
long as he lives in that world,

00:24:48.700 --> 00:24:50.510 align:middle line:90%
let him live in it.

00:24:50.510 --> 00:24:51.010 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:24:51.010 --> 00:24:54.220 align:middle line:84%
So here again,
the things started

00:24:54.220 --> 00:24:56.200 align:middle line:90%
to go different directions.

00:24:56.200 --> 00:24:58.750 align:middle line:90%


00:24:58.750 --> 00:25:01.180 align:middle line:84%
After being there for
three days doing nothing,

00:25:01.180 --> 00:25:03.730 align:middle line:84%
the fourth day, and I
came out at the weekend,

00:25:03.730 --> 00:25:06.290 align:middle line:84%
and started out on
a Monday morning.

00:25:06.290 --> 00:25:08.830 align:middle line:84%
We were called
out to go to work.

00:25:08.830 --> 00:25:14.650 align:middle line:84%
Our job was to clean bricks
from the broken buildings

00:25:14.650 --> 00:25:19.390 align:middle line:84%
and put them together on
trains, which in turn took them

00:25:19.390 --> 00:25:22.300 align:middle line:84%
to the Russian front
to build bunkers

00:25:22.300 --> 00:25:25.480 align:middle line:84%
for the winter for
the German army.

00:25:25.480 --> 00:25:27.040 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:25:27.040 --> 00:25:29.290 align:middle line:84%
Walking through the
streets from the job,

00:25:29.290 --> 00:25:35.920 align:middle line:84%
and from the job I read all
kinds of Jewish signatures,

00:25:35.920 --> 00:25:37.630 align:middle line:90%
Jewish sayings.

00:25:37.630 --> 00:25:38.800 align:middle line:90%
[NON-ENGLISH].

00:25:38.800 --> 00:25:41.980 align:middle line:90%


00:25:41.980 --> 00:25:43.120 align:middle line:90%
What does that mean?

00:25:43.120 --> 00:25:44.740 align:middle line:90%
We were betrayed.

00:25:44.740 --> 00:25:45.760 align:middle line:90%
I was here.

00:25:45.760 --> 00:25:47.238 align:middle line:90%
Like graffiti written on walls.

00:25:47.238 --> 00:25:48.030 align:middle line:90%
Yeah, on the walls.

00:25:48.030 --> 00:25:48.530 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:25:48.530 --> 00:25:49.720 align:middle line:90%
All right.

00:25:49.720 --> 00:25:52.270 align:middle line:84%
And I saw a street
[NON-ENGLISH],,

00:25:52.270 --> 00:25:54.850 align:middle line:90%
and another name of a street.

00:25:54.850 --> 00:25:55.570 align:middle line:90%
I didn't know.

00:25:55.570 --> 00:25:56.518 align:middle line:90%
I know that's Warsaw.

00:25:56.518 --> 00:25:57.310 align:middle line:90%
But I didn't know--

00:25:57.310 --> 00:25:59.110 align:middle line:84%
You didn't know that
this was the ghetto that

00:25:59.110 --> 00:25:59.875 align:middle line:90%
had been destroyed.

00:25:59.875 --> 00:26:00.280 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:26:00.280 --> 00:26:00.780 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:26:00.780 --> 00:26:03.545 align:middle line:84%
And I saw the big walls, and
I didn't know all of that.

00:26:03.545 --> 00:26:04.420 align:middle line:90%
We didn't understand.

00:26:04.420 --> 00:26:06.920 align:middle line:84%
You probably didn't even know
there had been a ghetto there.

00:26:06.920 --> 00:26:08.215 align:middle line:90%
Right, we didn't know that.

00:26:08.215 --> 00:26:08.715 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:26:08.715 --> 00:26:13.480 align:middle line:84%
So after going on like this two
weeks, finally we found out,

00:26:13.480 --> 00:26:16.420 align:middle line:84%
we came in contact
with the Polish people

00:26:16.420 --> 00:26:18.880 align:middle line:84%
there who have been
working, and being paid

00:26:18.880 --> 00:26:20.860 align:middle line:90%
by the Army for the Germans.

00:26:20.860 --> 00:26:24.160 align:middle line:84%
They said that this is the
section where the ghetto was.

00:26:24.160 --> 00:26:28.340 align:middle line:84%
And then one day, we went
from a different direction.

00:26:28.340 --> 00:26:29.660 align:middle line:90%
I passed by a big house.

00:26:29.660 --> 00:26:32.230 align:middle line:84%
There was a big sign
saying Judenrat.

00:26:32.230 --> 00:26:36.280 align:middle line:84%
So then I knew
that we were there.

00:26:36.280 --> 00:26:38.590 align:middle line:84%
So that was like
a Jewish council.

00:26:38.590 --> 00:26:40.690 align:middle line:84%
Judenrat, that was the
Jewish Council, right.

00:26:40.690 --> 00:26:43.060 align:middle line:84%
Yeah, the headquarters of
the Jewish Warsaw ghetto

00:26:43.060 --> 00:26:43.690 align:middle line:90%
Jewish council.

00:26:43.690 --> 00:26:45.130 align:middle line:90%
Right, OK.

00:26:45.130 --> 00:26:48.070 align:middle line:84%
So here I am, in
my wildest dreams

00:26:48.070 --> 00:26:50.440 align:middle line:84%
when I have dreamed
that here after six

00:26:50.440 --> 00:26:52.930 align:middle line:84%
months after the liquidation
of the Warsaw ghetto,

00:26:52.930 --> 00:26:55.600 align:middle line:84%
I'll be in there in
the Warsaw ghetto.

00:26:55.600 --> 00:26:58.570 align:middle line:90%
So we worked there.

00:26:58.570 --> 00:27:03.010 align:middle line:84%
One day, a German
comes over and he says,

00:27:03.010 --> 00:27:08.500 align:middle line:84%
a guard comes over and
he says, [NON-ENGLISH],,

00:27:08.500 --> 00:27:12.320 align:middle line:84%
which means who knows
how to read Yiddish?

00:27:12.320 --> 00:27:14.780 align:middle line:90%
So we had a saying.

00:27:14.780 --> 00:27:16.250 align:middle line:90%
And we had a rule.

00:27:16.250 --> 00:27:21.830 align:middle line:84%
Never volunteer for anything,
and never try to be alone.

00:27:21.830 --> 00:27:24.460 align:middle line:84%
Try to stay with
more people together.

00:27:24.460 --> 00:27:26.570 align:middle line:84%
Because whenever
anything happens,

00:27:26.570 --> 00:27:30.320 align:middle line:90%
first the fear is not there.

00:27:30.320 --> 00:27:34.970 align:middle line:84%
There's a lot of psychology
involved with that.

00:27:34.970 --> 00:27:37.020 align:middle line:90%
Nobody says nothing.

00:27:37.020 --> 00:27:41.690 align:middle line:90%
Then he says, [NON-ENGLISH].

00:27:41.690 --> 00:27:46.910 align:middle line:84%
There must be somebody be
who knows how to read Jewish.

00:27:46.910 --> 00:27:47.660 align:middle line:90%
You know?

00:27:47.660 --> 00:27:49.130 align:middle line:90%
So finally I said, yes.

00:27:49.130 --> 00:27:50.660 align:middle line:84%
I raised my hand,
and I says, yes.

00:27:50.660 --> 00:27:56.010 align:middle line:84%
So he comes and takes me away
and he says, come out here.

00:27:56.010 --> 00:27:56.970 align:middle line:90%
He calls me over.

00:27:56.970 --> 00:27:58.470 align:middle line:90%
I walked with him.

00:27:58.470 --> 00:28:02.160 align:middle line:84%
So another soldier comes
with him, one of the guards.

00:28:02.160 --> 00:28:03.360 align:middle line:90%
And I said uh-uh.

00:28:03.360 --> 00:28:04.630 align:middle line:90%
That's it.

00:28:04.630 --> 00:28:07.740 align:middle line:84%
And he took his machine gun off
from his hand, and we walked.

00:28:07.740 --> 00:28:11.400 align:middle line:84%
So some of my friends
said, that's it.

00:28:11.400 --> 00:28:13.470 align:middle line:84%
So he calls me aside,
and he takes me in front.

00:28:13.470 --> 00:28:17.160 align:middle line:84%
There's a bunker like
going down to the ground.

00:28:17.160 --> 00:28:21.270 align:middle line:90%
And it's with red paint to me.

00:28:21.270 --> 00:28:24.900 align:middle line:84%
Years later, down to me
that wasn't red paint.

00:28:24.900 --> 00:28:26.100 align:middle line:90%
It was blood.

00:28:26.100 --> 00:28:28.410 align:middle line:84%
But it looked like
dried paint, you know?

00:28:28.410 --> 00:28:29.760 align:middle line:90%
And you touch it, it falls off.

00:28:29.760 --> 00:28:30.420 align:middle line:90%
You know how?

00:28:30.420 --> 00:28:31.300 align:middle line:90%
Sure, flakes off.

00:28:31.300 --> 00:28:31.800 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:28:31.800 --> 00:28:34.170 align:middle line:84%
And it was written in
Jewish, in Yiddish,

00:28:34.170 --> 00:28:37.567 align:middle line:90%
it was written [NON-ENGLISH]

00:28:37.567 --> 00:28:38.400 align:middle line:90%
What does that mean?

00:28:38.400 --> 00:28:41.130 align:middle line:84%
In other words,
we were betrayed.

00:28:41.130 --> 00:28:43.680 align:middle line:90%
Remember us.

00:28:43.680 --> 00:28:48.750 align:middle line:84%
Later on, I found out that was
the headquarters of Anielewicz

00:28:48.750 --> 00:28:52.530 align:middle line:84%
and the whole gang of the
headquarters of the group who

00:28:52.530 --> 00:28:53.670 align:middle line:90%
fought to the last one.

00:28:53.670 --> 00:28:55.870 align:middle line:90%
So you translated that for him.

00:28:55.870 --> 00:28:58.030 align:middle line:84%
Yes, and I translated
it for him.

00:28:58.030 --> 00:29:00.640 align:middle line:84%
So he says to me,
what does it mean?

00:29:00.640 --> 00:29:07.450 align:middle line:84%
So I told him it means we were
forgotten, and remember us.

00:29:07.450 --> 00:29:08.710 align:middle line:90%
And he took me back there.

00:29:08.710 --> 00:29:10.000 align:middle line:90%
And it was over.

00:29:10.000 --> 00:29:10.690 align:middle line:90%
No problem.

00:29:10.690 --> 00:29:12.670 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:29:12.670 --> 00:29:14.410 align:middle line:90%
They gave us cigarettes.

00:29:14.410 --> 00:29:16.480 align:middle line:90%
We had the ration.

00:29:16.480 --> 00:29:23.770 align:middle line:84%
We had no-- so to speak,
besides the pushing

00:29:23.770 --> 00:29:26.570 align:middle line:84%
around and the hollering
in the usual way,

00:29:26.570 --> 00:29:29.890 align:middle line:90%
but nothing of the brutality.

00:29:29.890 --> 00:29:31.000 align:middle line:90%
Was it all men?

00:29:31.000 --> 00:29:32.800 align:middle line:90%
All men, no woman.

00:29:32.800 --> 00:29:35.350 align:middle line:84%
Nothing of a nature
of a brutality.

00:29:35.350 --> 00:29:37.080 align:middle line:84%
Were they Germans who
were guarding you?

00:29:37.080 --> 00:29:37.580 align:middle line:90%
Oh, yes.

00:29:37.580 --> 00:29:41.170 align:middle line:84%
There were Germans there
were Yugoslavs guarding us.

00:29:41.170 --> 00:29:43.360 align:middle line:84%
There was Polish
who was guarding us.

00:29:43.360 --> 00:29:45.880 align:middle line:90%
But they were civil to you.

00:29:45.880 --> 00:29:48.460 align:middle line:84%
Under the circumstances,
I would say, yes, nothing

00:29:48.460 --> 00:29:49.630 align:middle line:90%
of a cruelty or nothing.

00:29:49.630 --> 00:29:50.410 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:29:50.410 --> 00:29:56.310 align:middle line:84%
And the first
cruelty I entered was

00:29:56.310 --> 00:30:03.030 align:middle line:84%
one of my friends developed an
infection in one of his ears.

00:30:03.030 --> 00:30:07.560 align:middle line:84%
And some of the boys
said, don't go nowhere.

00:30:07.560 --> 00:30:09.720 align:middle line:90%
As long as you have it, stay.

00:30:09.720 --> 00:30:13.200 align:middle line:84%
Some of them said go to the
doctor and let them look at it.

00:30:13.200 --> 00:30:14.262 align:middle line:90%
He went to the doctor.

00:30:14.262 --> 00:30:14.970 align:middle line:90%
He took a chance.

00:30:14.970 --> 00:30:16.720 align:middle line:84%
The doctor looked
at him, and he says,

00:30:16.720 --> 00:30:18.630 align:middle line:90%
well, you got a bad infection.

00:30:18.630 --> 00:30:19.590 align:middle line:90%
There is nothing.

00:30:19.590 --> 00:30:20.760 align:middle line:90%
I have no medication.

00:30:20.760 --> 00:30:22.110 align:middle line:90%
There is nothing I can do.

00:30:22.110 --> 00:30:23.080 align:middle line:90%
Just take an aspirin.

00:30:23.080 --> 00:30:24.270 align:middle line:90%
He give him an aspirin.

00:30:24.270 --> 00:30:26.760 align:middle line:90%
But he needed antibiotics.

00:30:26.760 --> 00:30:29.820 align:middle line:84%
Well, there's nothing
I can do for you.

00:30:29.820 --> 00:30:31.940 align:middle line:90%
He got a high fever.

00:30:31.940 --> 00:30:34.830 align:middle line:84%
So the long story to make short,
he took him to the hospital.

00:30:34.830 --> 00:30:37.800 align:middle line:84%
There was a section that
he called a hospital.

00:30:37.800 --> 00:30:39.180 align:middle line:90%
He said, goodbye.

00:30:39.180 --> 00:30:41.530 align:middle line:84%
And that's the last time
I have ever seen him,

00:30:41.530 --> 00:30:43.392 align:middle line:84%
the last time I
ever heard of him.

00:30:43.392 --> 00:30:45.600 align:middle line:84%
Till this day, I don't know
what happened to him, how

00:30:45.600 --> 00:30:46.830 align:middle line:90%
he was killed or what.

00:30:46.830 --> 00:30:48.330 align:middle line:90%
But he disappeared.

00:30:48.330 --> 00:30:49.540 align:middle line:90%
That's it.

00:30:49.540 --> 00:30:52.080 align:middle line:90%
So that's the first encounter.

00:30:52.080 --> 00:30:55.800 align:middle line:84%
Second encounter was
a few days later,

00:30:55.800 --> 00:31:06.400 align:middle line:84%
an SS, a sergeant major, and
the rank of sergeant major

00:31:06.400 --> 00:31:09.430 align:middle line:90%
arrives on a motorbike.

00:31:09.430 --> 00:31:12.340 align:middle line:84%
And he says, we are
standing outside

00:31:12.340 --> 00:31:14.200 align:middle line:90%
in the field on the apellplatz.

00:31:14.200 --> 00:31:16.090 align:middle line:90%
And he says, good morning.

00:31:16.090 --> 00:31:19.030 align:middle line:90%
[GERMAN], who speaks German?

00:31:19.030 --> 00:31:21.940 align:middle line:84%
So several guys
raised their hands.

00:31:21.940 --> 00:31:22.930 align:middle line:90%
I was there too.

00:31:22.930 --> 00:31:24.340 align:middle line:90%
My father says, no don't go.

00:31:24.340 --> 00:31:26.380 align:middle line:90%
Don't go.

00:31:26.380 --> 00:31:29.410 align:middle line:84%
But I already raised
my hand, so I couldn't.

00:31:29.410 --> 00:31:32.380 align:middle line:84%
So he goes forwards,
to come forward.

00:31:32.380 --> 00:31:33.760 align:middle line:90%
I came forward.

00:31:33.760 --> 00:31:35.110 align:middle line:90%
He went to all of them through.

00:31:35.110 --> 00:31:35.890 align:middle line:90%
He came to me.

00:31:35.890 --> 00:31:39.100 align:middle line:84%
And he says to me,
how old are you?

00:31:39.100 --> 00:31:40.360 align:middle line:90%
[GERMAN]

00:31:40.360 --> 00:31:43.550 align:middle line:90%
I was siebzehn, 17.

00:31:43.550 --> 00:31:44.770 align:middle line:90%
He says, [NON-ENGLISH].

00:31:44.770 --> 00:31:46.360 align:middle line:90%
You'll be OK.

00:31:46.360 --> 00:31:48.190 align:middle line:90%
You'll do.

00:31:48.190 --> 00:31:49.340 align:middle line:90%
He says, come with me.

00:31:49.340 --> 00:31:50.890 align:middle line:90%
This was 1944?

00:31:50.890 --> 00:31:52.990 align:middle line:90%
Yeah.

00:31:52.990 --> 00:31:54.370 align:middle line:90%
In the beginning of '44.

00:31:54.370 --> 00:31:55.480 align:middle line:90%
Spring '44.

00:31:55.480 --> 00:31:56.710 align:middle line:90%
He says, come with me.

00:31:56.710 --> 00:31:58.870 align:middle line:90%
So you were really 19.

00:31:58.870 --> 00:32:00.100 align:middle line:90%
No, I'm already 18.

00:32:00.100 --> 00:32:00.940 align:middle line:90%
OK, whatever.

00:32:00.940 --> 00:32:02.540 align:middle line:90%
OK, yes, now I'm 18.

00:32:02.540 --> 00:32:05.588 align:middle line:90%
All right, he says come with me.

00:32:05.588 --> 00:32:07.220 align:middle line:90%
That was before my birthday.

00:32:07.220 --> 00:32:08.060 align:middle line:90%
All right, fine.

00:32:08.060 --> 00:32:09.620 align:middle line:90%
Yeah.

00:32:09.620 --> 00:32:10.370 align:middle line:90%
Achtzehn, yeah.

00:32:10.370 --> 00:32:11.360 align:middle line:90%
18.

00:32:11.360 --> 00:32:12.090 align:middle line:90%
Come with me.

00:32:12.090 --> 00:32:15.150 align:middle line:90%
So I went with him.

00:32:15.150 --> 00:32:17.990 align:middle line:90%
And he takes me to the front.

00:32:17.990 --> 00:32:22.340 align:middle line:84%
And he says there, he talks to
the sturmführer or something.

00:32:22.340 --> 00:32:24.650 align:middle line:90%
And then he says, come.

00:32:24.650 --> 00:32:27.948 align:middle line:84%
And I always, when you were
in camp and you talk to them,

00:32:27.948 --> 00:32:29.240 align:middle line:90%
you're not putting your hat on.

00:32:29.240 --> 00:32:30.560 align:middle line:90%
Your hat must be down.

00:32:30.560 --> 00:32:32.720 align:middle line:90%
So he says, put your hat down.

00:32:32.720 --> 00:32:33.560 align:middle line:90%
I put my hat down.

00:32:33.560 --> 00:32:35.930 align:middle line:84%
He says, sit in the
back of my motorbike.

00:32:35.930 --> 00:32:36.740 align:middle line:90%
So--

00:32:36.740 --> 00:32:38.992 align:middle line:84%
Were you wearing this
still this same uniform?

00:32:38.992 --> 00:32:41.450 align:middle line:84%
Sure, I was in uniform all the
time, the Auschwitz uniform.

00:32:41.450 --> 00:32:42.605 align:middle line:90%
Yeah, the prisoner uniform?

00:32:42.605 --> 00:32:43.580 align:middle line:90%
Yes, the uniform.

00:32:43.580 --> 00:32:45.800 align:middle line:90%
With the number here 845.

00:32:45.800 --> 00:32:49.020 align:middle line:84%
it's all the time,
nothing changed.

00:32:49.020 --> 00:32:54.330 align:middle line:84%
So he takes me and we
go several side streets.

00:32:54.330 --> 00:32:55.880 align:middle line:84%
And then he takes
me in a building.

00:32:55.880 --> 00:32:58.130 align:middle line:90%
And the building is bombed out.

00:32:58.130 --> 00:33:01.640 align:middle line:84%
But it's boarded
in from all over.

00:33:01.640 --> 00:33:03.390 align:middle line:84%
In other words, you
know like the windows.

00:33:03.390 --> 00:33:06.170 align:middle line:90%
They were all boarded in.

00:33:06.170 --> 00:33:09.490 align:middle line:90%
And it's a cold feeling to it.

00:33:09.490 --> 00:33:15.220 align:middle line:84%
It's something, it's like the
shivers and you walk in there.

00:33:15.220 --> 00:33:15.800 align:middle line:90%
I walk in.

00:33:15.800 --> 00:33:18.800 align:middle line:84%
And it's around, a big
building surrounded all around,

00:33:18.800 --> 00:33:22.430 align:middle line:84%
and in the middle it's
like a parking space.

00:33:22.430 --> 00:33:27.080 align:middle line:84%
There are trucks, cars,
half tracks, half tanks,

00:33:27.080 --> 00:33:28.370 align:middle line:90%
and all of that.

00:33:28.370 --> 00:33:30.930 align:middle line:84%
And it's bustling with
people coming and going.

00:33:30.930 --> 00:33:34.100 align:middle line:84%
And so he comes, takes me
in one of the sections,

00:33:34.100 --> 00:33:36.920 align:middle line:90%
takes me up and opens up a door.

00:33:36.920 --> 00:33:39.880 align:middle line:84%
And it's a big section
part of the building.

00:33:39.880 --> 00:33:41.060 align:middle line:90%
And there are dogs.

00:33:41.060 --> 00:33:42.500 align:middle line:90%
There are a dozen dogs.

00:33:42.500 --> 00:33:44.450 align:middle line:84%
And they're all barking,
and they're just

00:33:44.450 --> 00:33:46.170 align:middle line:84%
if he opens the
door, I'm finished,

00:33:46.170 --> 00:33:48.230 align:middle line:90%
they'll tear me apart.

00:33:48.230 --> 00:33:51.630 align:middle line:84%
And there is one dog
walking right behind him.

00:33:51.630 --> 00:33:56.845 align:middle line:84%
So he says to me in
German, he says, look.

00:33:56.845 --> 00:33:58.310 align:middle line:90%
He shows me.

00:33:58.310 --> 00:33:59.660 align:middle line:90%
There is a cage.

00:33:59.660 --> 00:34:02.860 align:middle line:84%
Between every dog
there is an empty cage.

00:34:02.860 --> 00:34:04.210 align:middle line:90%
There are cages.

00:34:04.210 --> 00:34:08.770 align:middle line:84%
There's two dogs, but in between
them is always an empty cage.

00:34:08.770 --> 00:34:10.434 align:middle line:90%
So he says to me like this.

00:34:10.434 --> 00:34:13.179 align:middle line:90%


00:34:13.179 --> 00:34:14.520 align:middle line:90%
You take this.

00:34:14.520 --> 00:34:16.830 align:middle line:84%
Open up this cage,
and open here.

00:34:16.830 --> 00:34:18.540 align:middle line:90%
This dog goes in here.

00:34:18.540 --> 00:34:19.889 align:middle line:90%
You close it back.

00:34:19.889 --> 00:34:23.520 align:middle line:84%
You clean this out,
put back in the food,

00:34:23.520 --> 00:34:24.780 align:middle line:90%
put in back the clean.

00:34:24.780 --> 00:34:28.679 align:middle line:84%
You open it up, the
dog goes back in.

00:34:28.679 --> 00:34:29.550 align:middle line:90%
And you open this--

00:34:29.550 --> 00:34:30.592 align:middle line:90%
So this was your new job.

00:34:30.592 --> 00:34:32.850 align:middle line:84%
Right, it was my job
to clean the cages

00:34:32.850 --> 00:34:34.650 align:middle line:90%
and give the dog the food.

00:34:34.650 --> 00:34:37.110 align:middle line:84%
And he says, you give
the dog the food.

00:34:37.110 --> 00:34:38.460 align:middle line:90%
But you don't eat his food.

00:34:38.460 --> 00:34:40.739 align:middle line:84%
He says, because you're
going to have plenty of food.

00:34:40.739 --> 00:34:42.440 align:middle line:90%
I says, fine.

00:34:42.440 --> 00:34:43.150 align:middle line:90%
[NON-ENGLISH].

00:34:43.150 --> 00:34:43.650 align:middle line:90%
Yeah.

00:34:43.650 --> 00:34:48.570 align:middle line:84%
Then he says to
me this dog here,

00:34:48.570 --> 00:34:53.699 align:middle line:84%
you can walk this way till
there, there was a line.

00:34:53.699 --> 00:34:58.020 align:middle line:84%
You can walk till there,
if you walk over the line,

00:34:58.020 --> 00:35:01.800 align:middle line:84%
there's a red line,
the dog will kill you.

00:35:01.800 --> 00:35:04.600 align:middle line:84%
And you can walk this
way till the red line.

00:35:04.600 --> 00:35:06.787 align:middle line:84%
If you walk over, the
dog will kill you again.

00:35:06.787 --> 00:35:08.370 align:middle line:84%
You know what kind
of dogs these were?

00:35:08.370 --> 00:35:11.080 align:middle line:84%
They were German shepherds,
but they were big--

00:35:11.080 --> 00:35:13.080 align:middle line:90%
Big dogs, big mean dogs.

00:35:13.080 --> 00:35:14.040 align:middle line:90%
Very mean.

00:35:14.040 --> 00:35:16.530 align:middle line:84%
They were-- some of them were
in black, and some of them

00:35:16.530 --> 00:35:20.070 align:middle line:90%
were-- it was the real McCoys.

00:35:20.070 --> 00:35:26.400 align:middle line:84%
And he said, if you go
this way, he'll jump you.

00:35:26.400 --> 00:35:28.980 align:middle line:84%
The only way you
can go is this here.

00:35:28.980 --> 00:35:29.730 align:middle line:90%
To do your job.

00:35:29.730 --> 00:35:30.230 align:middle line:90%
Yeah.

00:35:30.230 --> 00:35:33.083 align:middle line:84%
And he's going to
walk behind you.

00:35:33.083 --> 00:35:34.500 align:middle line:84%
And he's not going
to do anything.

00:35:34.500 --> 00:35:35.070 align:middle line:90%
They trained a dog.

00:35:35.070 --> 00:35:36.153 align:middle line:90%
They didn't need a person.

00:35:36.153 --> 00:35:38.250 align:middle line:84%
You can walk around any
place you want here,

00:35:38.250 --> 00:35:40.890 align:middle line:84%
but you cannot go there because
you'll jump you, and all that.

00:35:40.890 --> 00:35:41.932 align:middle line:90%
You can't cross the line.

00:35:41.932 --> 00:35:44.290 align:middle line:84%
The dog came and smelled me
a little bit and all that.

00:35:44.290 --> 00:35:48.921 align:middle line:84%
And so he says, I'll
come check with you back

00:35:48.921 --> 00:35:51.280 align:middle line:84%
in a [NON-ENGLISH],, which
means in about an hour.

00:35:51.280 --> 00:35:51.780 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:35:51.780 --> 00:35:57.570 align:middle line:84%
He came back in an hour
and he looked around.

00:35:57.570 --> 00:35:59.580 align:middle line:90%
He liked what I saw.

00:35:59.580 --> 00:36:02.940 align:middle line:84%
But doing the work,
I had a funny smell,

00:36:02.940 --> 00:36:06.930 align:middle line:84%
like a sweet smell that
I smelt in Auschwitz.

00:36:06.930 --> 00:36:09.630 align:middle line:84%
But I thought, ah, it
can't be the same smell.

00:36:09.630 --> 00:36:14.460 align:middle line:84%
It must be that from the
dogs, the stuff and all that,

00:36:14.460 --> 00:36:16.710 align:middle line:84%
the food, and the
odor and all that.

00:36:16.710 --> 00:36:18.750 align:middle line:90%
It must be from the dogs.

00:36:18.750 --> 00:36:23.248 align:middle line:84%
But somehow, I didn't I had a
funny feeling that it's not.

00:36:23.248 --> 00:36:23.790 align:middle line:90%
Well anyhow--

00:36:23.790 --> 00:36:26.188 align:middle line:84%
Well, this was on the
site of the Warsaw ghetto?

00:36:26.188 --> 00:36:28.230 align:middle line:84%
Yeah, inside, where the
Warsaw ghetto used to be.

00:36:28.230 --> 00:36:28.730 align:middle line:90%
Yeah, right.

00:36:28.730 --> 00:36:29.250 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:36:29.250 --> 00:36:31.260 align:middle line:90%
So I'm doing.

00:36:31.260 --> 00:36:31.897 align:middle line:90%
He comes back.

00:36:31.897 --> 00:36:32.730 align:middle line:90%
He looks at the job.

00:36:32.730 --> 00:36:34.350 align:middle line:90%
He says, job well done.

00:36:34.350 --> 00:36:35.730 align:middle line:90%
And it's lunch time.

00:36:35.730 --> 00:36:37.650 align:middle line:84%
He says, everybody's
eating lunch already.

00:36:37.650 --> 00:36:39.270 align:middle line:90%
He says you come with me.

00:36:39.270 --> 00:36:40.920 align:middle line:84%
He takes me to
the [NON-ENGLISH],,

00:36:40.920 --> 00:36:42.480 align:middle line:90%
to the kitchen there.

00:36:42.480 --> 00:36:45.300 align:middle line:84%
And he goes in and he says
to the guy in the kitchen,

00:36:45.300 --> 00:36:49.950 align:middle line:84%
[NON-ENGLISH] big
man, give him to eat.

00:36:49.950 --> 00:36:54.630 align:middle line:84%
So he comes up and he
says, [NON-ENGLISH],,

00:36:54.630 --> 00:36:56.420 align:middle line:90%
do you like noodles?

00:36:56.420 --> 00:36:57.150 align:middle line:90%
I says, yeah.

00:36:57.150 --> 00:36:57.970 align:middle line:90%
Oh, so.

00:36:57.970 --> 00:36:58.470 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:36:58.470 --> 00:37:02.040 align:middle line:84%
He brings me out a big
bowl loaded with noodles.

00:37:02.040 --> 00:37:03.600 align:middle line:90%
Why were they so good to you?

00:37:03.600 --> 00:37:05.580 align:middle line:90%
Me, because I worked there.

00:37:05.580 --> 00:37:07.230 align:middle line:90%
So for a working man, you know?

00:37:07.230 --> 00:37:09.090 align:middle line:90%
So I ate the noodles.

00:37:09.090 --> 00:37:10.780 align:middle line:90%
I couldn't eat up all of that.

00:37:10.780 --> 00:37:13.312 align:middle line:84%
So I just put in
my shirt down here,

00:37:13.312 --> 00:37:15.520 align:middle line:84%
and you're going to take it
to somebody who's hungry.

00:37:15.520 --> 00:37:17.530 align:middle line:84%
Took to my father,
I throw it in here.

00:37:17.530 --> 00:37:19.750 align:middle line:84%
You didn't know what
tomorrow was going to be.

00:37:19.750 --> 00:37:23.180 align:middle line:84%
Then he says to me,
stick around for a while.

00:37:23.180 --> 00:37:27.970 align:middle line:84%
And you help me clean my
[NON-ENGLISH],, the big kitchen.

00:37:27.970 --> 00:37:29.830 align:middle line:84%
And he says, I'll give
you some more to eat.

00:37:29.830 --> 00:37:30.820 align:middle line:90%
I said, fine.

00:37:30.820 --> 00:37:32.080 align:middle line:90%
I waited.

00:37:32.080 --> 00:37:34.900 align:middle line:84%
About a half an hour, the
other guy says to him, yeah,

00:37:34.900 --> 00:37:35.680 align:middle line:90%
[NON-ENGLISH].

00:37:35.680 --> 00:37:40.060 align:middle line:84%
The dog was next
to me watching me.

00:37:40.060 --> 00:37:42.220 align:middle line:84%
I cleaned up
everything beautiful.

00:37:42.220 --> 00:37:43.060 align:middle line:90%
He liked it.

00:37:43.060 --> 00:37:49.150 align:middle line:84%
He gave me a big canister, like
this loaded with chunks of meat

00:37:49.150 --> 00:37:51.640 align:middle line:90%
and all kind of macaroni.

00:37:51.640 --> 00:37:54.130 align:middle line:84%
And it came around 3 o'clock,
he says, come with me.

00:37:54.130 --> 00:37:57.130 align:middle line:84%
Put me on the bike, and
drove me back into the camp.

00:37:57.130 --> 00:38:00.460 align:middle line:84%
And that was been
going on like this

00:38:00.460 --> 00:38:02.890 align:middle line:90%
for about three or four weeks.

00:38:02.890 --> 00:38:05.573 align:middle line:84%
That's what made me survive
with my father and all that.

00:38:05.573 --> 00:38:06.490 align:middle line:90%
You brought food back.

00:38:06.490 --> 00:38:07.570 align:middle line:90%
I had plenty of food.

00:38:07.570 --> 00:38:10.010 align:middle line:84%
And I gave it to my uncles,
and some of my friends.

00:38:10.010 --> 00:38:11.410 align:middle line:90%
We had plenty of what to eat.

00:38:11.410 --> 00:38:13.780 align:middle line:84%
I couldn't get
rid of that smell.

00:38:13.780 --> 00:38:16.510 align:middle line:84%
And I says to my father, I don't
understand what's going on.

00:38:16.510 --> 00:38:17.570 align:middle line:90%
There is a smell.

00:38:17.570 --> 00:38:21.520 align:middle line:84%
And that taste of
the smell bugged me.

00:38:21.520 --> 00:38:22.020 align:middle line:90%
Sure.

00:38:22.020 --> 00:38:24.250 align:middle line:90%
It didn't let me.

00:38:24.250 --> 00:38:27.520 align:middle line:84%
And I know I had
smelled it somewhere.

00:38:27.520 --> 00:38:30.490 align:middle line:84%
One day, I don't know, after
being there for a while,

00:38:30.490 --> 00:38:34.700 align:middle line:84%
somehow he took the dog away or
something happened to the dog.

00:38:34.700 --> 00:38:36.400 align:middle line:90%
I can't explain how it happened.

00:38:36.400 --> 00:38:40.300 align:middle line:84%
The dog wasn't present
for quite a while.

00:38:40.300 --> 00:38:44.770 align:middle line:84%
And I heard some things
going on behind one wall.

00:38:44.770 --> 00:38:47.200 align:middle line:84%
I couldn't figure
it out for days

00:38:47.200 --> 00:38:48.920 align:middle line:84%
I knew that something
is going on.

00:38:48.920 --> 00:38:51.010 align:middle line:84%
So I thought then the
army is coming and going.

00:38:51.010 --> 00:38:53.500 align:middle line:90%
Sure.

00:38:53.500 --> 00:38:54.850 align:middle line:90%
Curiosity killed the cats.

00:38:54.850 --> 00:38:56.380 align:middle line:90%
And I wish I had never gone.

00:38:56.380 --> 00:38:58.510 align:middle line:90%
I wish I had never walked over--

00:38:58.510 --> 00:39:00.050 align:middle line:90%
Been curious.

00:39:00.050 --> 00:39:01.810 align:middle line:90%
I walked over.

00:39:01.810 --> 00:39:06.430 align:middle line:84%
And there was, they
had three cars.

00:39:06.430 --> 00:39:10.360 align:middle line:84%
In those days, the Germans used
to have like they have now,

00:39:10.360 --> 00:39:16.810 align:middle line:84%
the cars, the vans, big
vans like the parcel post

00:39:16.810 --> 00:39:18.500 align:middle line:90%
office is carrying, you know?

00:39:18.500 --> 00:39:19.000 align:middle line:90%
Sure.

00:39:19.000 --> 00:39:21.760 align:middle line:90%
Locked in, no windows, nothing.

00:39:21.760 --> 00:39:24.550 align:middle line:84%
They had like this,
colored in black.

00:39:24.550 --> 00:39:27.190 align:middle line:84%
And the Germans used
to pick up whoever

00:39:27.190 --> 00:39:28.810 align:middle line:90%
they were to pick up, the SS.

00:39:28.810 --> 00:39:32.513 align:middle line:84%
And threw them in, in those
wagons, and bring them there.

00:39:32.513 --> 00:39:34.930 align:middle line:84%
Meanwhile, your father and the
other people in this ghetto

00:39:34.930 --> 00:39:35.890 align:middle line:90%
were working too.

00:39:35.890 --> 00:39:36.160 align:middle line:90%
Yeah, they were working.

00:39:36.160 --> 00:39:37.270 align:middle line:90%
They had different jobs.

00:39:37.270 --> 00:39:39.542 align:middle line:84%
Yes, they have been
cleaning bricks, throwing.

00:39:39.542 --> 00:39:40.250 align:middle line:90%
Oh, that's right.

00:39:40.250 --> 00:39:43.360 align:middle line:84%
Yeah, they're working
on their bricks.

00:39:43.360 --> 00:39:47.110 align:middle line:84%
And some of them are working
in the fields with the farmers.

00:39:47.110 --> 00:39:49.205 align:middle line:84%
Each one has his own
job, and his own way.

00:39:49.205 --> 00:39:49.705 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:39:49.705 --> 00:39:52.470 align:middle line:90%


00:39:52.470 --> 00:39:54.600 align:middle line:84%
And then when I came
closer, and there

00:39:54.600 --> 00:39:57.870 align:middle line:84%
was a split between the
boards, put together,

00:39:57.870 --> 00:39:58.740 align:middle line:90%
there was openings.

00:39:58.740 --> 00:39:59.880 align:middle line:90%
So I could see.

00:39:59.880 --> 00:40:01.320 align:middle line:90%
In the back of this van?

00:40:01.320 --> 00:40:03.910 align:middle line:84%
In the back-- in the
backyard of that, you see?

00:40:03.910 --> 00:40:04.410 align:middle line:90%
Oh, I see.

00:40:04.410 --> 00:40:04.680 align:middle line:90%
I see.

00:40:04.680 --> 00:40:05.972 align:middle line:90%
You could see through the wall.

00:40:05.972 --> 00:40:08.040 align:middle line:90%
Wall, yeah, through the window.

00:40:08.040 --> 00:40:08.843 align:middle line:90%
It was boarded up.

00:40:08.843 --> 00:40:11.010 align:middle line:84%
Between the boards, you
could see on the other side.

00:40:11.010 --> 00:40:11.802 align:middle line:90%
You peeked through.

00:40:11.802 --> 00:40:12.302 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:40:12.302 --> 00:40:13.620 align:middle line:90%
And you could see what's there.

00:40:13.620 --> 00:40:16.200 align:middle line:84%
And there I saw
standing the three vans.

00:40:16.200 --> 00:40:22.680 align:middle line:84%
And on the van naked
people, tied their hands

00:40:22.680 --> 00:40:28.380 align:middle line:84%
and on their mouth they
had those taped up.

00:40:28.380 --> 00:40:29.370 align:middle line:90%
Taped.

00:40:29.370 --> 00:40:31.980 align:middle line:84%
They've been standing
like in a line.

00:40:31.980 --> 00:40:33.690 align:middle line:90%
And the smell--

00:40:33.690 --> 00:40:34.470 align:middle line:90%
On the street.

00:40:34.470 --> 00:40:38.812 align:middle line:90%
Standing in the yard.

00:40:38.812 --> 00:40:40.020 align:middle line:90%
In the courtyard or whatever.

00:40:40.020 --> 00:40:42.330 align:middle line:90%
Yeah, in that yard.

00:40:42.330 --> 00:40:45.510 align:middle line:84%
Then he took him,
picked them up,

00:40:45.510 --> 00:40:49.470 align:middle line:84%
and put him down like wood,
one by one, stacked them.

00:40:49.470 --> 00:40:52.320 align:middle line:84%
One here, one here,
one here, one here.

00:40:52.320 --> 00:40:53.490 align:middle line:90%
They were not living?

00:40:53.490 --> 00:40:55.320 align:middle line:90%
Yeah, alive people.

00:40:55.320 --> 00:40:57.570 align:middle line:90%
They were standing.

00:40:57.570 --> 00:41:00.120 align:middle line:84%
But their hands were
tied in the back.

00:41:00.120 --> 00:41:02.520 align:middle line:84%
Well, who picked-- you mean
they were picking up bodily.

00:41:02.520 --> 00:41:03.060 align:middle line:90%
Two guys picked them up.

00:41:03.060 --> 00:41:03.810 align:middle line:90%
With their legs--

00:41:03.810 --> 00:41:06.330 align:middle line:84%
One grabbed them by the legs
and the other like this.

00:41:06.330 --> 00:41:08.368 align:middle line:84%
There were women, and
they were, I don't

00:41:08.368 --> 00:41:09.660 align:middle line:90%
know if they were old or young.

00:41:09.660 --> 00:41:11.730 align:middle line:84%
But I could see the difference
between men and women.

00:41:11.730 --> 00:41:12.230 align:middle line:90%
Of course.

00:41:12.230 --> 00:41:15.630 align:middle line:84%
Yeah, and they put them
down stacked them like this.

00:41:15.630 --> 00:41:17.880 align:middle line:84%
Two this way, and
two on top of them.

00:41:17.880 --> 00:41:19.942 align:middle line:84%
And again, they made it
three, sometimes four.

00:41:19.942 --> 00:41:21.150 align:middle line:90%
They lay them down, you mean?

00:41:21.150 --> 00:41:22.410 align:middle line:90%
Right, like wood.

00:41:22.410 --> 00:41:23.310 align:middle line:90%
Yeah, OK.

00:41:23.310 --> 00:41:24.060 align:middle line:90%
They grabbed them.

00:41:24.060 --> 00:41:26.250 align:middle line:84%
They were tied, their legs
and everything was tied.

00:41:26.250 --> 00:41:26.950 align:middle line:90%
And they were standing.

00:41:26.950 --> 00:41:29.170 align:middle line:84%
And their mouths were taped,
so there were no sounds.

00:41:29.170 --> 00:41:29.920 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:41:29.920 --> 00:41:30.880 align:middle line:90%
And they put them down.

00:41:30.880 --> 00:41:33.520 align:middle line:84%
And another guy came in
and threw full of gasoline

00:41:33.520 --> 00:41:34.510 align:middle line:90%
on top of them.

00:41:34.510 --> 00:41:35.530 align:middle line:90%
You saw this.

00:41:35.530 --> 00:41:38.830 align:middle line:90%
Oh, how terrible.

00:41:38.830 --> 00:41:39.910 align:middle line:90%
I didn't know what to do.

00:41:39.910 --> 00:41:43.720 align:middle line:84%
As soon as I saw that, the
first reaction came to me, now

00:41:43.720 --> 00:41:44.500 align:middle line:90%
I know the smell.

00:41:44.500 --> 00:41:50.260 align:middle line:84%
That's from Auschwitz,
the corpse smell.

00:41:50.260 --> 00:41:51.400 align:middle line:90%
And I went back.

00:41:51.400 --> 00:41:52.880 align:middle line:90%
I couldn't move.

00:41:52.880 --> 00:41:55.490 align:middle line:90%
I couldn't talk.

00:41:55.490 --> 00:42:00.500 align:middle line:84%
And he came in, and he
said what's [NON-ENGLISH]..

00:42:00.500 --> 00:42:02.280 align:middle line:90%
He recognized on my face.

00:42:02.280 --> 00:42:03.650 align:middle line:90%
He said what happened?

00:42:03.650 --> 00:42:04.437 align:middle line:90%
What's going on?

00:42:04.437 --> 00:42:05.270 align:middle line:90%
This is your father?

00:42:05.270 --> 00:42:07.100 align:middle line:90%
No, my-- the SS.

00:42:07.100 --> 00:42:07.720 align:middle line:90%
Oh, I see.

00:42:07.720 --> 00:42:10.800 align:middle line:90%
The SS man came back with a dog.

00:42:10.800 --> 00:42:11.790 align:middle line:90%
He saw your shock.

00:42:11.790 --> 00:42:12.290 align:middle line:90%
He saw me.

00:42:12.290 --> 00:42:14.640 align:middle line:90%
You're in the state of shock.

00:42:14.640 --> 00:42:16.050 align:middle line:90%
I didn't know what to answer.

00:42:16.050 --> 00:42:18.790 align:middle line:84%
So I says, I made like
this, and holding my hand.

00:42:18.790 --> 00:42:22.580 align:middle line:84%
And I says the dog
had me [NON-ENGLISH]..

00:42:22.580 --> 00:42:25.770 align:middle line:84%
In other words, the dog
almost [NON-ENGLISH] me.

00:42:25.770 --> 00:42:26.270 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:42:26.270 --> 00:42:29.490 align:middle line:84%
And he took my hand and looked
down, and said, [NON-ENGLISH]..

00:42:29.490 --> 00:42:31.730 align:middle line:84%
Yeah, I says, I took
it away in time.

00:42:31.730 --> 00:42:35.300 align:middle line:84%
He have this inside
[NON-ENGLISH]..

00:42:35.300 --> 00:42:36.290 align:middle line:90%
That's what I got.

00:42:36.290 --> 00:42:38.000 align:middle line:90%
Yeah.

00:42:38.000 --> 00:42:39.710 align:middle line:84%
You didn't want to
tell him what you saw.

00:42:39.710 --> 00:42:40.210 align:middle line:90%
Right.

00:42:40.210 --> 00:42:42.267 align:middle line:90%
He says, [NON-ENGLISH]?

00:42:42.267 --> 00:42:43.100 align:middle line:90%
What does that mean?

00:42:43.100 --> 00:42:43.760 align:middle line:90%
Did you see anything?

00:42:43.760 --> 00:42:44.810 align:middle line:90%
Did you hear anything?

00:42:44.810 --> 00:42:46.160 align:middle line:90%
I says, no.

00:42:46.160 --> 00:42:47.750 align:middle line:90%
Nothing.

00:42:47.750 --> 00:42:48.560 align:middle line:90%
OK.

00:42:48.560 --> 00:42:51.593 align:middle line:84%
So he took me in
and came in the camp

00:42:51.593 --> 00:42:52.760 align:middle line:90%
back, and came to my father.

00:42:52.760 --> 00:42:53.690 align:middle line:90%
And my father saw me.

00:42:53.690 --> 00:42:56.640 align:middle line:84%
He says, what's the
matter with you?

00:42:56.640 --> 00:42:57.370 align:middle line:90%
So I told him.

00:42:57.370 --> 00:42:59.500 align:middle line:84%
I don't know if they are
Jews or who they are.

00:42:59.500 --> 00:43:01.860 align:middle line:90%
I don't know.

00:43:01.860 --> 00:43:04.690 align:middle line:90%
And I couldn't eat.

00:43:04.690 --> 00:43:05.730 align:middle line:90%
I couldn't sleep.

00:43:05.730 --> 00:43:09.160 align:middle line:84%
At night, the more
I thought about it,

00:43:09.160 --> 00:43:11.010 align:middle line:84%
the more it started
to bother me.

00:43:11.010 --> 00:43:14.760 align:middle line:84%
And then it dawned on me
at night, I says, my God.

00:43:14.760 --> 00:43:19.860 align:middle line:84%
Can you imagine the pain
those people had to go through

00:43:19.860 --> 00:43:25.590 align:middle line:84%
by not even taking away from
them their most human thing

00:43:25.590 --> 00:43:29.280 align:middle line:84%
that even you are not
allowed to scream and cry

00:43:29.280 --> 00:43:30.870 align:middle line:90%
in your own pain.

00:43:30.870 --> 00:43:33.000 align:middle line:84%
You can't do this to
the worst to an animal.

00:43:33.000 --> 00:43:34.860 align:middle line:90%
Who are those people?

00:43:34.860 --> 00:43:38.490 align:middle line:84%
To this day, I don't know who
they are, and what they are.

00:43:38.490 --> 00:43:41.350 align:middle line:84%
I never knew, probably
will never know.

00:43:41.350 --> 00:43:43.330 align:middle line:90%
But it went on day after day.

00:43:43.330 --> 00:43:44.370 align:middle line:90%
I saw this once.

00:43:44.370 --> 00:43:45.660 align:middle line:90%
That was happened one time.

00:43:45.660 --> 00:43:49.002 align:middle line:84%
So I assume it went on, because
the smell was constantly there.

00:43:49.002 --> 00:43:51.210 align:middle line:84%
The smell was there when I
came there the first time.

00:43:51.210 --> 00:43:53.817 align:middle line:84%
Did you see them light
a flame to this gas?

00:43:53.817 --> 00:43:55.650 align:middle line:84%
They threw gasoline and
threw a match to it.

00:43:55.650 --> 00:43:58.078 align:middle line:90%
Like, that's it.

00:43:58.078 --> 00:44:00.120 align:middle line:84%
OK, so how long were did
you stay in this ghetto?

00:44:00.120 --> 00:44:01.453 align:middle line:90%
And we were standing like this--

00:44:01.453 --> 00:44:08.890 align:middle line:84%
and there was all kinds of
things, smelling and all

00:44:08.890 --> 00:44:09.440 align:middle line:90%
of that.

00:44:09.440 --> 00:44:12.945 align:middle line:84%
And it was going on,
it's already June.

00:44:12.945 --> 00:44:15.070 align:middle line:84%
It has been going on like
this all the way to July.

00:44:15.070 --> 00:44:18.640 align:middle line:84%
In August we heard
some shootings going on

00:44:18.640 --> 00:44:23.510 align:middle line:84%
and rumors that the Russians
are approaching Warsaw,

00:44:23.510 --> 00:44:27.670 align:middle line:84%
and that we will be
liberated by the Russians.

00:44:27.670 --> 00:44:30.460 align:middle line:84%
And at one night, we
heard a lot of shooting,

00:44:30.460 --> 00:44:34.180 align:middle line:84%
a lot of explosions,
a lot of stuff.

00:44:34.180 --> 00:44:38.140 align:middle line:84%
Rumors had it that
the Polish underground

00:44:38.140 --> 00:44:41.680 align:middle line:84%
tried to break in, in the
camp and to liberate us.

00:44:41.680 --> 00:44:44.780 align:middle line:84%
But they were beaten back
and they couldn't make it.

00:44:44.780 --> 00:44:49.570 align:middle line:84%
The next day, I had another
taste of good stuff.

00:44:49.570 --> 00:44:53.500 align:middle line:84%
We got up in the morning and
we announced that this lager

00:44:53.500 --> 00:44:55.060 align:middle line:90%
will be dissolved.

00:44:55.060 --> 00:44:56.500 align:middle line:90%
And we were going to be--

00:44:56.500 --> 00:44:58.090 align:middle line:90%
What does that word mean lager?

00:44:58.090 --> 00:44:59.310 align:middle line:90%
Lager means camp.

00:44:59.310 --> 00:44:59.920 align:middle line:90%
Camp, OK.

00:44:59.920 --> 00:45:01.568 align:middle line:90%
That camp will be dissolved.

00:45:01.568 --> 00:45:02.860 align:middle line:90%
You're going to be moved again.

00:45:02.860 --> 00:45:04.450 align:middle line:84%
And we will be
moved from the camp.

00:45:04.450 --> 00:45:05.740 align:middle line:90%
We are going to Germany.

00:45:05.740 --> 00:45:07.990 align:middle line:90%
Oh, OK.

00:45:07.990 --> 00:45:10.180 align:middle line:84%
But we didn't know that
we were going to walk.

00:45:10.180 --> 00:45:11.638 align:middle line:84%
We thought that we
were going to be

00:45:11.638 --> 00:45:14.590 align:middle line:84%
taken to transport, you know,
and transport to another camp.

00:45:14.590 --> 00:45:15.220 align:middle line:90%
Sure.

00:45:15.220 --> 00:45:16.270 align:middle line:90%
We got up in the morning.

00:45:16.270 --> 00:45:19.660 align:middle line:84%
We stood there from the
morning from 4 o'clock

00:45:19.660 --> 00:45:25.160 align:middle line:84%
till 10:30 at night on the day
outside, no water, no food,

00:45:25.160 --> 00:45:26.980 align:middle line:90%
nothing, all day long.

00:45:26.980 --> 00:45:29.740 align:middle line:84%
Then we were told to go
back into the barracks.

00:45:29.740 --> 00:45:31.970 align:middle line:84%
That was already 18
hours you're standing.

00:45:31.970 --> 00:45:32.470 align:middle line:90%
Yeah.

00:45:32.470 --> 00:45:33.580 align:middle line:90%
So we went back in.

00:45:33.580 --> 00:45:34.520 align:middle line:90%
We went to sleep.

00:45:34.520 --> 00:45:37.420 align:middle line:84%
The next day at 4 o'clock
in the morning, again out.

00:45:37.420 --> 00:45:42.610 align:middle line:84%
We were standing outside
again all day, sun is shining.

00:45:42.610 --> 00:45:45.920 align:middle line:84%
It looked like even heaven
came down against us.

00:45:45.920 --> 00:45:48.910 align:middle line:84%
It was a beautiful day, hot
and muggy, and everything.

00:45:48.910 --> 00:45:50.770 align:middle line:90%
No water, no nothing.

00:45:50.770 --> 00:45:52.450 align:middle line:90%
There is collapsing a guy.

00:45:52.450 --> 00:45:53.920 align:middle line:90%
Here is collapsing a guy.

00:45:53.920 --> 00:45:58.150 align:middle line:84%
Take him away,
never see him again.

00:45:58.150 --> 00:46:00.850 align:middle line:84%
Needless to say, that the
shoving and the screaming

00:46:00.850 --> 00:46:05.290 align:middle line:84%
and the hollering what has been
going on is constantly there.

00:46:05.290 --> 00:46:09.490 align:middle line:84%
The pushing and the
brutalizing reached a point

00:46:09.490 --> 00:46:12.130 align:middle line:84%
where it doesn't matter anymore
with you, because you're

00:46:12.130 --> 00:46:13.060 align:middle line:90%
already used to it.

00:46:13.060 --> 00:46:15.670 align:middle line:84%
So you take it as an
everyday occurring.

00:46:15.670 --> 00:46:16.670 align:middle line:90%
That's the way it is.

00:46:16.670 --> 00:46:20.270 align:middle line:90%
It doesn't go any other way.

00:46:20.270 --> 00:46:24.760 align:middle line:84%
Finally, the third day
here we are for two days

00:46:24.760 --> 00:46:28.330 align:middle line:84%
standing like this outside,
without food, without water,

00:46:28.330 --> 00:46:29.230 align:middle line:90%
tired.

00:46:29.230 --> 00:46:30.840 align:middle line:84%
They gave you food when
you went into the barrack

00:46:30.840 --> 00:46:31.510 align:middle line:90%
at night though.

00:46:31.510 --> 00:46:32.260 align:middle line:90%
No, no, nothing.

00:46:32.260 --> 00:46:33.730 align:middle line:90%
This is three days with no food.

00:46:33.730 --> 00:46:35.420 align:middle line:84%
That's the two
days without food,

00:46:35.420 --> 00:46:36.550 align:middle line:90%
without water, or anything.

00:46:36.550 --> 00:46:39.730 align:middle line:84%
The third day in the morning,
we got up at 4 o'clock.

00:46:39.730 --> 00:46:41.830 align:middle line:84%
We stand outside again
till around 9:00,

00:46:41.830 --> 00:46:43.330 align:middle line:90%
9:30 in the morning.

00:46:43.330 --> 00:46:45.550 align:middle line:90%
Then they bring in.

00:46:45.550 --> 00:46:46.640 align:middle line:90%
We got in line.

00:46:46.640 --> 00:46:53.780 align:middle line:84%
Everybody get a Herring, a
salt Herring, a half a bread,

00:46:53.780 --> 00:46:59.590 align:middle line:84%
two slices of margarine, and
two slices of cut of jelly,

00:46:59.590 --> 00:47:02.980 align:middle line:90%
and a big soup.

00:47:02.980 --> 00:47:05.425 align:middle line:84%
And of course, being hungry
and thirsty and everything.

00:47:05.425 --> 00:47:06.070 align:middle line:90%
You eat everything, of course.

00:47:06.070 --> 00:47:07.250 align:middle line:90%
Eat everything up.

00:47:07.250 --> 00:47:09.760 align:middle line:84%
Two hours later, we
are on the march.

00:47:09.760 --> 00:47:12.820 align:middle line:90%
We are starting to go.

00:47:12.820 --> 00:47:16.450 align:middle line:84%
How everything was
figured out, now the salty

00:47:16.450 --> 00:47:20.320 align:middle line:84%
Herring after eating,
everybody eating everything

00:47:20.320 --> 00:47:26.170 align:middle line:84%
up, and walking in the heat,
starts to work for water.

00:47:26.170 --> 00:47:29.770 align:middle line:90%
Water, water, no water.

00:47:29.770 --> 00:47:31.570 align:middle line:90%
Just keep on walking.

00:47:31.570 --> 00:47:33.020 align:middle line:84%
Anybody, all of a
sudden you hear.

00:47:33.020 --> 00:47:33.520 align:middle line:90%
Psst.

00:47:33.520 --> 00:47:34.450 align:middle line:90%
Shot.

00:47:34.450 --> 00:47:38.260 align:middle line:84%
Anybody stays behind,
left behind, shot.

00:47:38.260 --> 00:47:39.610 align:middle line:90%
Throw it on a wagon.

00:47:39.610 --> 00:47:42.250 align:middle line:84%
Some of them, that's
the first days.

00:47:42.250 --> 00:47:45.340 align:middle line:84%
The first two days, everybody
got shot was thrown on a wagon.

00:47:45.340 --> 00:47:47.830 align:middle line:90%
At night, were buried.

00:47:47.830 --> 00:47:51.117 align:middle line:84%
Later on, you didn't even
bother to pick him up anymore.

00:47:51.117 --> 00:47:52.450 align:middle line:90%
You just left him on the street.

00:47:52.450 --> 00:47:54.830 align:middle line:90%
So you walked for how many days?

00:47:54.830 --> 00:47:57.370 align:middle line:90%
Do you remember?

00:47:57.370 --> 00:47:58.720 align:middle line:90%
We walked from Warsaw.

00:47:58.720 --> 00:48:01.120 align:middle line:84%
We walked to a little
village called Kutna.

00:48:01.120 --> 00:48:04.690 align:middle line:84%
It was on the Czechoslovakian
and Polish border.

00:48:04.690 --> 00:48:08.920 align:middle line:84%
We walked for almost, let's
see for about between 8 and 10

00:48:08.920 --> 00:48:11.320 align:middle line:90%
days.

00:48:11.320 --> 00:48:14.265 align:middle line:84%
One day, the fifth day,
we reached a river.

00:48:14.265 --> 00:48:17.620 align:middle line:90%


00:48:17.620 --> 00:48:20.920 align:middle line:84%
When we got to the river,
everybody jumped in

00:48:20.920 --> 00:48:22.620 align:middle line:90%
and drinking water.

00:48:22.620 --> 00:48:28.600 align:middle line:90%
We had another encounter.

00:48:28.600 --> 00:48:33.340 align:middle line:84%
They had the Gestapo,
not the Gestapo,

00:48:33.340 --> 00:48:37.150 align:middle line:84%
but the SS, the
guards and the kapos,

00:48:37.150 --> 00:48:39.640 align:middle line:84%
if a guy were there
drinking water,

00:48:39.640 --> 00:48:42.460 align:middle line:84%
he just went,
stepped on his neck.

00:48:42.460 --> 00:48:43.540 align:middle line:90%
That's the end.

00:48:43.540 --> 00:48:45.640 align:middle line:84%
And stood there as
long as he could,

00:48:45.640 --> 00:48:47.770 align:middle line:84%
let him, till he
tell suffocated.

00:48:47.770 --> 00:48:50.350 align:middle line:84%
Tell me, how many of
you were on this march?

00:48:50.350 --> 00:48:51.340 align:middle line:90%
Do you have any idea?

00:48:51.340 --> 00:48:53.710 align:middle line:90%
Yes, I will come to that.

00:48:53.710 --> 00:48:58.450 align:middle line:84%
We started out close
to 10,000 from Warsaw.

00:48:58.450 --> 00:49:02.570 align:middle line:84%
We arrived less
than 8,000 to Kutna.

00:49:02.570 --> 00:49:06.230 align:middle line:84%
In Kutna they brought
in again a train.

00:49:06.230 --> 00:49:08.270 align:middle line:90%
And this was 10 days later?

00:49:08.270 --> 00:49:08.930 align:middle line:90%
Yes.

00:49:08.930 --> 00:49:15.830 align:middle line:84%
OK, and the ninth day
without water, God

00:49:15.830 --> 00:49:18.410 align:middle line:84%
opened up the heavens
and it started to rain.

00:49:18.410 --> 00:49:21.980 align:middle line:84%
I was wet, not my
skin from the outside,

00:49:21.980 --> 00:49:24.230 align:middle line:90%
but already from the inside.

00:49:24.230 --> 00:49:28.070 align:middle line:84%
Even the heavens
were against us.

00:49:28.070 --> 00:49:32.840 align:middle line:84%
And you can imagine how
we have been here sitting

00:49:32.840 --> 00:49:36.470 align:middle line:84%
walking and we were
tired, in the throes,

00:49:36.470 --> 00:49:43.070 align:middle line:84%
and by a farmer there in
the field outside to rest,

00:49:43.070 --> 00:49:45.830 align:middle line:84%
we had to lay down in
the mud and all of this,

00:49:45.830 --> 00:49:51.800 align:middle line:84%
and sitting there for two
days, again without food.

00:49:51.800 --> 00:49:54.590 align:middle line:84%
Finally, third day
in the morning,

00:49:54.590 --> 00:49:58.380 align:middle line:84%
they gave us some
bread and some soup.

00:49:58.380 --> 00:49:59.030 align:middle line:90%
We had to go.

00:49:59.030 --> 00:49:59.690 align:middle line:90%
The train came.

00:49:59.690 --> 00:50:02.697 align:middle line:84%
We had to go in a train,
again, the cattle wagons.

00:50:02.697 --> 00:50:04.280 align:middle line:84%
And you don't know
where you're going.

00:50:04.280 --> 00:50:06.230 align:middle line:90%
Oh, we don't know.

00:50:06.230 --> 00:50:08.600 align:middle line:84%
We only know that
we are by seeing it,

00:50:08.600 --> 00:50:10.490 align:middle line:84%
we weren't told where
we are, just what

00:50:10.490 --> 00:50:14.508 align:middle line:84%
we could make out from our own
just figuring it out and seeing

00:50:14.508 --> 00:50:15.050 align:middle line:90%
where we are.

00:50:15.050 --> 00:50:16.760 align:middle line:90%
We saw the sign saying Kutna.

00:50:16.760 --> 00:50:20.480 align:middle line:84%
We know that we are in Kutna,
on the border what's what.

00:50:20.480 --> 00:50:25.430 align:middle line:84%
And being there for about
a day, after we were

00:50:25.430 --> 00:50:27.860 align:middle line:90%
put in, in the wagons.

00:50:27.860 --> 00:50:29.030 align:middle line:90%
The wagons were closed.

00:50:29.030 --> 00:50:30.140 align:middle line:90%
The doors were locked.

00:50:30.140 --> 00:50:31.130 align:middle line:90%
And away we go.

00:50:31.130 --> 00:50:35.010 align:middle line:84%
We don't know
where we are going.

00:50:35.010 --> 00:50:39.780 align:middle line:84%
My gosh, if this is hell,
if there is hell on Earth,

00:50:39.780 --> 00:50:41.580 align:middle line:90%
that sure was hell.

00:50:41.580 --> 00:50:46.590 align:middle line:84%
We were about 120 pressed
into a cattle wagon.

00:50:46.590 --> 00:50:49.050 align:middle line:84%
And the clothes,
everybody was wet,

00:50:49.050 --> 00:50:51.600 align:middle line:84%
and it was sticky
and muddy outside.

00:50:51.600 --> 00:50:54.070 align:middle line:90%
And we started the feeling.

00:50:54.070 --> 00:50:59.700 align:middle line:84%
And at night, they come in,
and with whips and shooting,

00:50:59.700 --> 00:51:03.300 align:middle line:90%
and hitting, and clubbing.

00:51:03.300 --> 00:51:04.740 align:middle line:90%
God knows what.

00:51:04.740 --> 00:51:05.370 align:middle line:90%
It's dark.

00:51:05.370 --> 00:51:06.150 align:middle line:90%
We can't see.

00:51:06.150 --> 00:51:07.590 align:middle line:90%
We don't know.

00:51:07.590 --> 00:51:08.660 align:middle line:90%
I got hit with--

00:51:08.660 --> 00:51:11.550 align:middle line:90%
I don't even know what it was.

00:51:11.550 --> 00:51:15.960 align:middle line:84%
In the daytime, I saw the guy
he had a tail from a horse

00:51:15.960 --> 00:51:17.400 align:middle line:90%
dried out.

00:51:17.400 --> 00:51:18.870 align:middle line:90%
He used it like a whip.

00:51:18.870 --> 00:51:21.540 align:middle line:84%
And I got hit with
that on the head.

00:51:21.540 --> 00:51:26.760 align:middle line:84%
And in the morning,
we look around there.

00:51:26.760 --> 00:51:28.440 align:middle line:90%
Is a guy shot.

00:51:28.440 --> 00:51:30.900 align:middle line:90%
There is a guy beaten to death.

00:51:30.900 --> 00:51:33.510 align:middle line:90%
There is a guy died.

00:51:33.510 --> 00:51:35.620 align:middle line:84%
To make the long story
short, by the time

00:51:35.620 --> 00:51:41.125 align:middle line:84%
we arrived from Kutna to
Dachau, which took us all night

00:51:41.125 --> 00:51:47.350 align:middle line:84%
and a little bit of the day,
from the 8,000 or so left,

00:51:47.350 --> 00:51:53.200 align:middle line:84%
and from beginning
from we arrived 2,000

00:51:53.200 --> 00:51:57.040 align:middle line:90%
and some few hundred of us.

00:51:57.040 --> 00:52:01.390 align:middle line:84%
Lucky, my father and
my uncle, my uncle

00:52:01.390 --> 00:52:02.570 align:middle line:90%
was beaten on the head.

00:52:02.570 --> 00:52:05.120 align:middle line:84%
But he was bleeding,
but he survived.

00:52:05.120 --> 00:52:07.870 align:middle line:90%
So we arrived in Dachau.

00:52:07.870 --> 00:52:09.870 align:middle line:90%
Your father survived this?

00:52:09.870 --> 00:52:11.170 align:middle line:90%
Yes, we survived.

00:52:11.170 --> 00:52:12.100 align:middle line:90%
We all came in.

00:52:12.100 --> 00:52:15.370 align:middle line:84%
But there was others who we
knew didn't make it, friends.

00:52:15.370 --> 00:52:17.770 align:middle line:84%
And so why do you think that
the Germans took you away

00:52:17.770 --> 00:52:19.930 align:middle line:84%
from that ghetto, because
the Russians were coming,

00:52:19.930 --> 00:52:20.805 align:middle line:90%
and they didn't want?

00:52:20.805 --> 00:52:24.010 align:middle line:84%
Yes, the Russians already
prepared their attack

00:52:24.010 --> 00:52:25.540 align:middle line:90%
against Warsaw.

00:52:25.540 --> 00:52:26.920 align:middle line:90%
And it was just approaching.

00:52:26.920 --> 00:52:29.630 align:middle line:84%
And they didn't want us
to be liberated by them.

00:52:29.630 --> 00:52:30.130 align:middle line:90%
Sure.

00:52:30.130 --> 00:52:31.120 align:middle line:90%
They needed you workers.

00:52:31.120 --> 00:52:32.620 align:middle line:84%
They wanted you to
continue working.

00:52:32.620 --> 00:52:34.150 align:middle line:90%
Right, so they took us back in.

00:52:34.150 --> 00:52:36.180 align:middle line:90%
They took us into Dachau.

00:52:36.180 --> 00:52:37.410 align:middle line:90%
We arrived to Dachau.

00:52:37.410 --> 00:52:39.690 align:middle line:84%
Dachau was already
crowded, because they

00:52:39.690 --> 00:52:43.350 align:middle line:84%
started to bring in
from outside the people.

00:52:43.350 --> 00:52:48.690 align:middle line:84%
And the first thing they
gave us a shower, to bathe

00:52:48.690 --> 00:52:52.478 align:middle line:90%
and took away our clothes.

00:52:52.478 --> 00:52:55.470 align:middle line:84%
They took away our clothes
and give us new clothes.

00:52:55.470 --> 00:52:58.830 align:middle line:84%
And they gave us a
pair of wooden shoes.

00:52:58.830 --> 00:53:02.700 align:middle line:90%
And they let us stay.

00:53:02.700 --> 00:53:05.220 align:middle line:84%
They gave us food,
just like for the rest

00:53:05.220 --> 00:53:08.820 align:middle line:84%
of the prisoners
in the camp, once

00:53:08.820 --> 00:53:12.600 align:middle line:84%
a day water in the morning like
tea, and a soup in the evening,

00:53:12.600 --> 00:53:14.080 align:middle line:90%
and all of that.

00:53:14.080 --> 00:53:16.590 align:middle line:90%
And we stayed there.

00:53:16.590 --> 00:53:20.520 align:middle line:84%
We had where to sleep, at least
like regular barracks and all

00:53:20.520 --> 00:53:21.180 align:middle line:90%
of that.

00:53:21.180 --> 00:53:22.080 align:middle line:90%
All right.

00:53:22.080 --> 00:53:25.260 align:middle line:84%
Let's take a break
again now Larry,

00:53:25.260 --> 00:53:30.120 align:middle line:84%
and we'll get back to it, to
the rest of your experiences

00:53:30.120 --> 00:53:31.550 align:middle line:90%
in Dachau in a few minutes.

00:53:31.550 --> 00:53:32.050 align:middle line:90%
All right.

00:53:32.050 --> 00:53:34.760 align:middle line:84%
Let's wait till
the lights go out.

00:53:34.760 --> 00:53:58.000 align:middle line:90%